var e=[{version:`0.8.1`,date:`2026-11-10`,changes:[`Vehicles move smoothly on a big map even while the simulation cannot keep up: the map is drawn a moment behind the simulation and takes in what it sends as it gets there, at the pace it really runs, so a vehicle you follow no longer stops and jumps every few frames (at 40x on a giant map it stood in one frame of every six)`,`Trains glide at 10x and 40x instead of going by leaps: between two looks of the simulation a train was drawn moving only if it had gone less than 12 m, which at 40x it nearly never had`,`Buses, lorries and cars at high speed and far from the view move evenly: each move is drawn over the time it took, not over the last step of the traffic, where it stood most of the time and then leapt`,`The windows that redraw as the game runs (lines, vehicles, finance, a town, an industry) take turns, one a frame, instead of all in the same frame every quarter of a second`,`Zooming with the wheel is smoother: what keeps its size on the screen (signals, lines, overlays, the names of places) is drawn again every second step of the zoom while it moves, and at the exact one once it stands; with the Lines window open the lines are drawn again a few at a time, not all in one frame`,`For the makers: node scripts/fast.mjs --worst 8 lists the frames of most main-thread work of each view, part by part`,`For the makers: node scripts/smooth.mjs follows a bus and a train and looks at a town at 1x, 10x and 40x, and says how evenly the frames come and how evenly what is drawn moves in them (docs/PERFORMANCE.md)`]},{version:`0.8.0`,date:`2026-11-10`,changes:[`The settings are one window with tabs along the top, in the main menu and in a game: General, Game, Sound, Graphics, Keys, Statistics, Versions and Privacy. Statistics moved there from the main menu, What's new opens the Versions tab, and the settings have a cog. The desktop app has a Quit button, in the main menu and under General, which saves the game first`,`A YouTube video in news of the makers or the notes of a version shows as its picture with a play button; a click plays it large over the game, and Escape or a click beside it closes it. The game on CrazyGames shows the link only`,`A town's car park in the way of what you build is cleared, as houses are: it shows red before you build, costs $18,000, and the town minds it as much as three houses. It is gone for good, its ground left open. Before, a vehicle depot or anything else could be built on top of a car park and both stayed; a car park under a depot built that way is gone now too (#125)`,`At traffic lights the cars of a queue follow each other through on green: each one no longer stops dead short of the junction as the car ahead drives out of it, and then pulls away from a stand again, so more cars get through on each green and the queues at lights are shorter`,`For the makers: a cleanup before 0.8.0: two functions of the simulation nothing called are gone, as are names it offered that nothing used, the checks for extending the track of a station at either end are written once, and the client uses the place hash of the simulation and one order of squares for drawing; the game is the same`,`With a station, stop, hub or depot selected, or the Lines, a town's or another window open, the game runs smoother at high speed: their cards are worked out a few times a second instead of in every frame, the Lines window updates only the rows that changed, and the bar at the top costs a third of what it did; they look the same`,`Cars no longer vanish at dead-end streets: a car parked facing the dead end, or sent into one, turns round at its end and drives out again (about 35 cars a day were lost so on a big map, now one or two); pnpm jams also shows for the makers what is left over at 3:00 each day, and why cars were lost`,`A town that razes a block draws again only the squares of the map round it: the buildings, their lights at night, the car parks and gardens, the dirt tracks, the fences and the parking at the kerb are drawn square by square, and a square where nothing changed keeps what it was drawn as; where people walk is worked out again only where the roads changed. It looks the same, and a raze takes about half the time and memory it did`,`Trains in a bend are no longer drawn anew in every frame: each car is kept as a drawing of its own and turned with the track, as buses are; they look the same, and from a region at 40x the computer has about a third less to do each frame`,`For the makers: scripts/fast.mjs says how many drawing commands (fills and strokes) the page made a second in each view`,`For the makers: scripts/fast.mjs takes --query to add to the address of the page, such as traffic=threads to send every step to the traffic workers`,`For the makers: the traffic workers keep their copies of the world for far less: each step they are sent only what the step reads (of the buses and lorries only those it can meet and only what it reads of them, sent while the workers get ready), the simulation's own thread takes a larger share where it waited for them, a change of the roads is worked out again by the workers while the simulation steps that one alone, and before a road opens they find the ways over it ahead; still slower than one thread on the maps of today, so they still wait for a step big enough`,`At high speed the building sites in view draw their ground no more than five times a second, and their crews about 30 times a second, instead of in every frame; it looks the same`,`In a time lapse the light streaks of the cars are drawn about 30 times a second while the view stands still, not in every frame: they move too fast to follow either way, and a big city in view leaves the computer a good deal more time for the rest`,`From far off at high speed the map no longer redraws its pictures of the land as fast as something under them changes: a change there shows within a second or two, and a big map running at 40x has about a fifth less to do each frame; it looks the same`,`For the makers: in the desktop app the traffic can step on worker threads of its own beside the simulation, each with a copy of the world kept by patches and the cars in shared memory, the same game on any number of them (tested to the last car on 1 to 4 threads); measured slower than one thread on the maps of today, so it waits for a step big enough, and the Profiling tab shows each traffic worker`,`For the makers: pnpm dev:isolated starts the game isolated across origins as the desktop app is, so memory is shared and the traffic workers can run (with ?traffic=threads in the address every step goes to them); the traffic workers now also run in Chrome, which may not write text straight into shared memory`,`For the makers: each thread of the traffic keeps what it writes beyond its own areas (car park spots given, buses and lorries at their stops, distances driven) in a log of its own, put together after the step by area, then by id; the game is the same to the last car`,`For the makers: in the desktop app the cars and what moves of the buses, lorries and trains now lie in memory that several threads can share, ready for the traffic to run on more than one; the game, its saves and its fingerprint are exactly the same, and the traffic is checked to come out the same however its areas are shared out to threads`,`A town that takes down a block to build anew no longer has the whole map worked out and drawn again: what is built (track, stations, the roads and what stands on them) is kept as it was, and only the scenery makes room again, with what lies far from the block kept from the time before. On a big map such a redraw takes about half the time and makes about half the garbage it did, so the game stutters less at high speed; it looks the same.`,`The levels of Simulation detail are now Low, Medium and Custom. Low (what Standard was) is the browser's, Low of every part with nobody on foot; Medium (desktop app) is Medium of every part and where a new map starts there; Custom (what Detailed was) sets each part by itself, starting at Medium. A Detailed game of before plays on as Custom at the High it had`,`Simulation detail is a button in the New map form and in the Game settings, showing the level; it opens a window of its own with the level and, under it, every part of it to choose from. At Standard the parts show what it plays and cannot be pressed. In a running game of the desktop app the level can now be changed too: to Detailed it keeps what was played until you change a part, back to Standard it plays Standard's set again`,`Detailed simulation (desktop app) is set part by part: under the level in the New map form, and in the Game settings of a running game, choose Low, Medium or High for Cars, Household size, Greenery and Countryside, and Off to High for People on foot. Detailed starts at High for each. Standard plays one set: Low for each, so a big map in the browser has fewer cars than before (a car for 430 people, at most 1,300), and nobody on foot is simulated one by one any more (the people on the pavements are still drawn). In the browser the knobs show with a lock. In a running game fewer cars lets those on the road finish their trips, People on foot Off ends the walks under way, a new household size is for households made from then on, and greenery and countryside are drawn anew at once. Saves of before keep their level as it played`,`For the makers: the traffic now steps area by area, in squares of 512 m, each area seeing the others as they were when the step began, so the game comes out the same whatever order the areas step in: the ground for running the traffic on several threads. Everything drives by the same rules; a car or bus driving out of a junction into another area is handed over once its tail is clear of that junction, and a bus or lorry that reaches its stop or dock arrives at the end of the step`,`Big cities have real traffic: how many cars may drive at once now grows with the people of the towns, a car for every 285 people at Standard (every 107 at Detailed), instead of 450 (800) for the whole map whatever its size. A new map starts with as many as before; a map of 32 towns has about four times as many cars on its roads at rush hour, and far fewer trips are turned away for want of room`,`For the makers: the Profiling tab of the developer tools says which thread each part runs on (the simulation in its worker, the frame on the main thread), and a new Helpers section shows each helper thread with the jobs it ran over the last 30 seconds by kind, how long the last and the average took, and how long the simulation waited for an answer`,`On a big map the traffic takes less of each tick: where you look, and what an open window watches (a vehicle, the line shown, a town), every car, bus and lorry drives as before; farther off they move every fourth step, by the same rules and all the time they are owed, so none is lost and jams still form. Saves keep where you looked`,`Rail signals stay as big as they are as you zoom out, instead of growing on the map, and fade out once they are small; traffic lights and the barriers of level crossings fade out too, and the forklifts at works fade in instead of appearing at once. What has faded out is not drawn at all`,`On a big map the towns and the passengers hold the simulation less: what each town has of its needs (lines, waiting, noise, air, goods, power) is measured for all towns at once on a helper thread and counted ten minutes of the game later; how busy its streets are is still measured on the spot`,`Rail signals keep their size on the screen as you zoom out, instead of shrinking with the map, and then fade out over a stretch of the zoom; traffic lights and the barriers of level crossings fade out too, and the forklifts at works fade in instead of appearing at once. What has faded out is not drawn at all`,`A road built or taken away, and a town that builds, hold the simulation a little less: the parking at the kerb, the car parks and where the cars of each district start no longer look up for every road and road node of the map which district it lies in, only where the districts changed, and a car park finds its road again only where a road changed near it`,`The traffic takes about a tenth less of each step on a big map, with every car, bus and lorry driving exactly as before: what each asks of the roads, junctions, lights and level crossings as it drives is looked up in plain tables instead of in maps and objects, and the trains are looked for only on track that a road crosses`,`With a vehicle selected the game runs smoother: the moving arrows along its line are drawn once and kept instead of anew in every frame, and the Vehicles window updates only the rows that changed instead of the whole list, which made a stutter several times a second with many vehicles`,`A big game at high speed makes far less garbage for the browser to clear, so the pauses for that come less often: the signals and traffic lights are drawn again at most four times a second, not every frame a train passes one; the loaders of freight yards are moved, not drawn anew; those who wait at a station are drawn again only there; and what is under the pointer is looked for ten times a second, near the pointer only`,`At a stop by the kerb a bus or a tram now stands with its middle at the stop, beside the pole and the shelter, instead of with its front there, and the yellow box of the stop is centred on it. In a bay a bus stands as before`,`One-way bus and tram stops: set Ways to One in the build bar and click on the side of the road the stop is to stand. Buses and trams call there only driving that way, and a line coming the other way turns round to come back by it. Two one-way stops of the two ways may stand opposite each other as a pair, a stop on a one-way road is always one-way (they can now stand there), and a slip road takes none. A one-way stop has its pole, shelter and box on its own side only, and its line shows the way it is called at instead of a choice of side`,`The strip down the middle of a divided road has trees, bushes, both or only grass, by stretches, the same each time. A Custom road with a median has pavements and people walking along it like a street, and no fence; a crossing over it leaves the strip out and lays a piece of pavement there, and an island stop on the strip has a crossing at each end of it`,`Tram tracks in the roads are drawn thinner and a little fainter, over the lines and the boxes of the stops instead of under them`,`Bus stops show where their vehicles stand: a box with a zigzag in each lane a bus or a tram stops in, as long as the longest vehicle of the lines that call there, so a stop of a tram line is as long as a tram, and in the lane by the middle where its tracks are. A stop on a divided Custom road is now allowed, and has an island with a shelter on the strip where a bus/tram lane runs beside it. BUS is no longer painted on bus/tram lanes nor at stops`,`Bus lanes are now bus/tram lanes. In the Custom road window a side can have two of them, each by the kerb or by the middle: a tram line down the middle of an avenue with a bus lane at its kerb, or two bus lanes side by side. Buses keep to the one nearest the kerb and tram tracks lie in the one nearest the middle; with one, both share it as before. A tram now keeps to its tracks through a junction instead of following the lane connections of the buses or moving to the lane of its turn`,`A junction whose traffic lights leave a connected turn red in every phase has a yellow ! over it on the map: what drives there waits for ever, and the card of the junction says how many turns it is`,`Two lorries or long buses no longer stand across each other in the middle of a junction for good, with queues on every arm: of two that turn left from opposite sides and would meet, one now waits for the other, and one let through to clear a jam gets going at once instead of handing its turn back and forth. A car bound for a parking spot on a street it may not turn into from where it came, by the lanes you connected, now parks elsewhere instead of waiting at that turn for ever`,`Telling all towns at once to build no longer stops the game on a big map: each order had everything the game works out from the roads and towns worked out again, which on a map of 32 towns held the simulation for close to a minute until the game restarted it. Now only what the town built is worked out again`,`A lane or a house a town builds no longer has the ways of every train to the lines that may borrow it searched again: those go by the track, the stations and the lines only`,`At high speed on a big map the simulation sends the screen less each time: of a town only the counts that changed, not all its lots, and of who rides in a train or bus nothing unless someone got on or off`,`Zoomed out over the whole map of a big game the frames are smoother: what moves is listed for the graphics card apart from what stands, and the cars in traffic, a third of a pixel from there, fade out and are no longer worked out by day (their lights still show at night). The trains, buses and lorries turn into a few strokes in the colours of their lines there, which look the same from so far and cost the graphics card a fraction. Zooming in, the trees no longer change at once from far-off dots to crowns: the crowns come in over a stretch of the zoom and fade in tile by tile. In line mode and build mode zooming is smoother: your vehicles over the line are kept drawings, moved, and the pins of the bus stops are one drawing placed for each stop, not drawn anew in every frame`,`While towns build on a big map the screen keeps a smoother frame rate: the car parks and the docks the drawing reads come from the simulation thread, which has them already, instead of being worked out again on the thread that draws, with the whole demand and network behind them`,`For developers: the bench of the tick can time the simulation as the game is built (pnpm bench --bundled), not only as Vite loads it while developing, which made every call between files slower than in the game`,`For developers: the bench of the tick times a played game at 40×, ticks back to back against the 1.25 ms each has, and says how fast this computer could run it`,`Building no longer makes the screen stop for a moment while the roads, pavements, track, stations and buildings are drawn again: their shapes are made on a thread of their own, and the old picture stays until the new one is ready`,`Zooming is smoother, most of all in build mode: the hatching of the yards is drawn once and kept, and from far off is a faint fill as dark as it was; the signals and the power lines are made on that thread as the zoom changes; and the lights of the cars, the pins of the stops and the marks of the traffic lights are no longer drawn again while nothing moves`,`Zooming in line mode is smoother: the stops of the line and your vehicles over its way are drawn again only when the zoom has passed a step or a vehicle moved, not in every frame`,`Zoomed out over the whole map or a region, the map is drawn from pictures of it, baked by area and baked again where something changes, instead of from millions of shapes, and the lights of the buildings at night are one glow each: far quicker on a weak graphics card, and it looks the same. The cars at the kerb and in car parks show from a little nearer than before`,`For developers: pnpm render times drawing the map alone: the game stands still while the camera flies the same path over a save in every theme, at night, in build mode and in line mode, with the work of each frame, the draw calls, the corners sent to the graphics card and what Pixi made into triangles`,`At high speed on a big map the traffic takes about a third less of each tick and throws away less than half the memory it did: the queues of the lanes, what holds up a road and what the junctions keep track of are tables of numbers kept from one step to the next, and what stays the same from step to step is no longer looked up again. Every car, bus and lorry drives exactly as before`,`When a town builds at night or a road is built or taken away, the game holds less long: the car parks on the land of buildings are laid out again only near what changed, the kerb spots kept clear only for the roads whose ways in changed, the districts of a town found about twice as fast, and the trips between halts no longer written out pair by pair`,`A road taken away or built holds the game less long: the ways over the roads, the docks and the junctions are worked out again only where it changed them, and the cars, buses and trams keep the ways they found where those never went over the road taken away`,`A town builds what it found at night 20 minutes of the game after it looked, not 5: at the highest speed the game no longer stops to wait for a town that took long to look`,`When a town begins an industry in its estate, the network of the lines, the docks and the halts are no longer worked out again: only what an industry is part of`,`For developers: the bench of the tick has a third case, a street the player builds across a block of a town`,`For developers: pnpm bench --worst N plays each case N times and gives each tick the least of its times, by phase: numbers that hold beside other work on the computer`,`Buses and lorries out of view no longer make the page fail now and then: a shadow kept for one that was hidden could be thrown away while its drawing still held it`,`At high speed on a big map the game stutters less when towns build or roads open: the cars parked are worked out again a little each frame instead of all at once, and what is under works, the signals and the map drawn again wait for the next frame where one has no time left`,`In a time lapse the streaks of the cars and the lights at night cost the browser less: their drawing keeps the room it needs from frame to frame, and a streak is worked out without lists thrown away for each of its points`,`Where working out the cars parked goes wrong once, they are worked out again in the next frame instead of the map stopping and with it the game`,`For developers: pnpm soak says an error of the page as it happens, and a run whose game has stopped ends with an error instead of waiting for ever`,`For developers: pnpm soak --cpu --long 12 says what the stretches of work of 12 ms and more went on, and keeps the profile to open in Chrome`,`A street built in a town holds the game about a third less long: the ways the cars keep make room for the new roads once instead of at every road built, and the car parks on the land of buildings are looked up without making a name for them each time`,`A road taken away holds the game less long: the ways the cars keep find again what went over it from a list of what leads on from each road, made once, not looked up for every way`,`A town measured right after it built holds the game less long: how many of its trips go by train or bus is added up without writing out each pair of halts, and the blocks it kept are not named again`,`A road built or taken away no longer looks for every level crossing of the map again, only where a road it changed had one or crosses track`,`The car parks of stations are laid out again only where a road changed near them, and the streets a town reaches are found without working out the distance to every crossing of the map`,`After a town builds, where people go is worked out about twice as fast, and the district of each crossing of the streets is kept for the towns whose land did not change`,`After the roads change, the cars parked at the kerb where a spot is gone are found asking each road once, not once for every car`,`When a town begins an industry in its estate, the power lines are no longer laid out again over the whole map unless the industry stands where a line goes: on a big map that was a stop of a tenth of a second or more`,`A town building at night holds the game about half as long: it puts in what it built on a tick the traffic does not move, and the kerb spots and the spots on the land of buildings it did away with are freed a tick later, so the work is shared over two ticks`,`A line can no longer be changed between bus and tram while it has vehicles, not even by taking all its stops away first: a bus could end up on a tram line, a tram on a bus line`,`A tram bought without a line goes only into a vehicle depot with tram tracks at its gate, and a bus or lorry not into one on tracks for trams alone`,`A line changed to Tram drops its waypoints that are off the tram tracks, instead of drawing that part of the line as broken`,`A tram no longer turns round where it stands when a crossing laid by hand lies a little way short of the end of its tracks: the crossing laid by itself at the end stays`,`A tram turning back over a crossing while a road is built across its street no longer ends up beside the road, and a tram in a jam turns back only where its tracks end`,`Trams no longer pull off their rails into a bus bay: a bay can be a stop of a tram line, also one in a saved game, but the tram drives past it and nobody gets on or off it there; no bay is built on tracks for trams alone`,`Laying tram tracks along a road takes down only the houses within that road's own width, not a tramway's`,`Demolish takes the nearest tram crossing wherever along it you click, and a click on the crossing laid by itself at the end of the tracks no longer takes the road away`,`A tram put back after its road is split lands on a road with tracks, and a damaged save with broken tram crossings or a broken turn of a tram loads mended`,`At high speed on a big map the passengers and the towns take less of each tick: what a journey draws is kept until one of its lines runs otherwise, and how many of a town's trips go by train or bus is counted again only when the hour or one of those lines changed. The game plays exactly as before`]},{version:`0.7.6`,date:`2026-11-07`,changes:[`Where the helper threads of the simulation all stop, the game no longer keeps an ever longer list of changes for them, and the copy they work on is compared whole at every job`,`On a map with more than 144 towns every town ends its day again: those past the 144th were never judged and never grew. The towns are measured one a tick instead of all in one tick, and the end of a town's day no longer works out again the halts and journeys of all the map when only its people changed, so a big map stutters less through the day and at night`,`On big maps the frames go more smoothly: the map takes in only what the simulation changed since the frame before, and works out the cars, the people on foot and the trains only near the view, the cars parked again only in the car parks where one came or went, and the traffic lights only when one of them turns`,`The cars parked on the land of buildings are drawn again without looking for their car park each time one comes or goes`,`The simulation tells the screen what changed of the car parks, the parked cars and the books of past days where it changes them, instead of comparing all of them every frame, and after a town builds or works open it compares only what they can have changed: a frame costs the simulation about half as much on a big map`,`While developing, the game checks every half second that the simulation told the screen of every change of the car parks, stations and stops, and says so in the console where it did not`,`The simulation also tells the screen which stations and stops changed (who waits there, their rating, their yard) instead of comparing every one of them every frame`,`Building on a big map stutters less: the trees, houses and gardens that make room for what is built find what is near them several times quicker`,`And with less of the work done again: the strips of parking at the kerb are kept for each road, the people on foot find the next stretch of pavement by where it is, and the ways into the courts find the strips they open into the same way`,`When a town begins or finishes an industry, the land is laid out and drawn again in less than half the time: on a big map that was a second or more in which the game stood still. Drawing the map again after something was built stops more often between its parts, so a frame waits less on it`,`What is built is drawn in sooner and with less for the graphics to make: of the roads, pavements, buildings and ground drawn again, only the patches of the map that changed are made anew, the rest of the picture is kept, and telling which is which is spread over the frames`,`The trees, houses, gardens and dirt tracks make room for something built only near where it was built: on a big map that is two to three times quicker`,`When a town begins or finishes an industry, the land is laid out again a little each frame while the map as it was stays on the screen, and then takes its place: the game no longer stands still for it`,`When a town lays a lane or a road is taken away, the districts are worked out again only for the town whose roads changed, and the roads near a place are found by where they lie instead of by looking at every road of the map: the tick of a new lane is shorter on big maps`,`A lane a town lays, still under works, no longer has the ways over the roads, the docks of lorries and buses, the level crossings and the bus stops worked out again where it changes none of them`,`A lane a town lays works out again only the junctions it meets, not all of them`,`When a town builds, the districts, the demand between the places and the car parks on the land of buildings are worked out again only for what changed: the screen no longer stops for a long frame on big maps when a town builds, and the tick of a new lane is shorter`,`Taking a road away no longer works out again what follows from the stations and the lines alone, such as the journeys between the halts`]},{version:`0.7.5`,date:`2026-11-07`,changes:[`The code that moves traffic along the roads is split into smaller parts: the game plays exactly as before`,`The code that draws the map and clears the scenery for what you build is split into smaller parts: nothing looks or plays differently`,`Maps lay out their houses, gardens, car parks and the order of traffic lights with the same sums on every computer, so a game plays out the same in any browser`,`The list of what changed in each version loads when the Versions window opens instead of with the game, so the game starts with about 110 kB less to download`,`A waypoint set on the map goes at the end of the list of stops again, as a new stop does, or after the stop chosen in the list: drag it to put it elsewhere`,`The text of a dropdown, such as How on the Journeys map, no longer has the bottoms of its letters cut off`,`The button for vehicle depots in the build bar is called Vehicle depot, no longer Depot like the one of trains, and the tutorial rings it when it asks for one. In build mode, line mode and the analytics the radio and the newspaper step aside, and the radio plays on`]},{version:`0.7.4`,date:`2026-11-05`,changes:[`A junction without lights where traffic stood still no longer lets through only one car at a time for hours: of those stuck, the one that has waited longest goes first, so a car from a side road that stopped across a busy main road goes on and no longer holds up the rest`,`Download save and saving under a name no longer write a save without its households when the simulation is too busy to give one: the game says it could not save just now, and says so once too when the autosave gets none. A save with no version still gets its news, lane connections, traffic lights and tram crossings, and the warnings of a line in the Lines window no longer work out the ways by its other platforms, which they never showed`,`Lorries no longer stand for good round a loop of short roads where they turn round: one let through a stuck junction drives on out of it while there is room on its own road, even with the road after it full; one already on its way out no longer counts its own body as no room; and a bus or a lorry goes into a dead end only with room to come back out of it, instead of standing in one with others on the way back`,`The Custom road window lays out a road lane by lane: its lanes are cards across the road under a picture of it, dragged along the row to move them, over the middle to turn them round and off the row to take them out, and Lane, Bus lane and Median are dragged or clicked in. Custom in the road menu is now New, with a plus, at its right end. Save as road keeps a road under a name as a button of its own in the road menu, with an icon of its own, set apart from the kinds of road by a line, in every game: pick it to build it, and Set opens it to change, rename, duplicate or delete it. A custom road has no Bus or One-way in the build bar: its bus lanes and its ways are set in its window. Its speed limit is a sign at the top left of the picture, which you click to choose another, with its width and price at the top right; the build bar shows its speed limit as a sign too`,`Trams: Tram in the Road group of the build bar opens a menu: Tram lays tram tracks, in the outermost lane of the roads you draw it along, or as tracks of their own off them, rails on the ground, fenced where houses are near. A tram line calls at the bus stops on its tracks, and its waypoints lie on them too: pick Tram in its Stops window. Trams start in a vehicle depot on a road with tracks, each of whose bays gets rails of its own by itself, curving out into the tracks of the road towards its gate, and they drive in and out on them car by car; they carry 150 people, their three cars follow the tracks round a curve one behind the other, they have a cab at each end but never turn round where they stand: they turn back over a scissors crossing between the two tracks, backing over one behind them or driving over one ahead into the stub beyond. Scissors in the Tram menu lays one, shown as you place it, and every end of tram tracks has one by itself. A bus stop on tram tracks of their own is for trams alone, no parking stands beside them, and towns build no street on to them`]},{version:`0.7.3`,date:`2026-11-04`,changes:[`Tracks side by side that cross a road close together share one level crossing: one set of barriers over all of them, closed while a train comes on any of them. Cars and buses drive on to a level crossing only when there is room past it, so none waits between the tracks or on the rails`,`A junction can no longer lock up for good: a bus or a lorry that has waited long at the line goes into a full junction only where there is room for all of it on the far side, instead of stopping across it with its way out full, one that cannot go out no longer keeps the others of the junction waiting behind it, and buses and lorries that came out of a junction side by side into the same lane no longer stand stacked at its mouth for good. A bus or a lorry told to be sold that has no road to any depot or parking is sold where it stands, and a worn-out vehicle on its way to a depot no longer says it has none`,`Lorries call at a lorry stop on a hub from the road its bays open on to, and from a quieter street on the other side of that road only where nothing else leads there: they no longer stand with no way to a stop when such a street is built beside it`,`A town whose houses are full but whose satisfaction is below what it needs to build shows Full under Houses in its window, with the satisfaction it builds from, and A day no longer counts people who find no room. The wiki says from what satisfaction people move in and from what a town builds`,`Where a Custom road with more lanes one way than the other runs on into a piece laid the other way round, its lines no longer jump a lane sideways at the joint: the line down the middle, the lane lines and the bus lanes move across into those of the next piece`,`A sound stopped before it began to play is no longer sent to the makers as an error of the game`,`Two lines can no longer have the same name: a name another line has, in any case, turns red as you type it and is not kept, and a new line gets a number no line has yet. Lines of a saved game that share a name keep it until you rename one`,`On a very big map, a game that waits long for the plans of a town or of the traffic is given up to a minute before it goes back to its last save, instead of 15 seconds: going back only came to the same wait again. Autosaves no longer pile up while one is still waiting, so the game stands still less often, and what you build while the game is paused no longer waits for the next thing you do when an autosave was under way. For the makers: a report that the simulation stopped says which kind of stop it was and how long its ticks, its helpers and its saves took`]},{version:`0.7.2`,date:`2026-11-01`,changes:[`In the schedule overview, − and + beside Weekday or Weekend change every part of that day at once, and Copy schedule and Paste schedule put the whole schedule of one line onto others; Copy weekday to weekend is now Copy to weekend. The lists of the schedule overview use the scrollbars of the game, a little wider in every window`,`The schedule overview lists your lines on the left, with search, vehicle types and a filter, and a warning beside a line that has an issue now; the line you pick shows a card for each part of a weekday and of the weekend, with a bar of how many ride on its busiest stretch against a dashed line of the seats your vehicles give, a button that copies weekdays to the weekend, what needs doing now, and the vehicles that work it`,`Houses you take down are gone for good: they never come back, even when what you built there is taken away, and the town never builds on that ground again. The people who lived there move away, and the town holds it against you for about a month. Under a bridge the houses stay standing`,`Cars held up in a jam wait an hour of the game, not ten minutes, before they look for another way, and then take another road before they ever turn round: turning round is the last way out`,`Buses and lorries held up at a junction for a while no longer drive into the one standing ahead of them and stay stuck inside it`,`On a road with a bus lane, buses keep to it for a turn either way and queue in it one behind the other, instead of pulling out beside each other and blocking the turn`,`Bus lanes are lanes in the junction editor: they have square dots, their connections are dashed, and they can be connected like any other lane. Buses and the lorries of your lines follow them, from a bus lane into a car lane or from a car lane into a bus lane; cars never turn into a bus lane`,`At traffic lights, cars and buses on green follow each other through instead of crossing one at a time as at a stop sign, and those going straight no longer give way to left turns from the other side: a left turn waits in the junction and goes when the other way stops at amber or red`,`Changing the green time of a phase of traffic lights right after taking a phase out no longer stops the game with an error`,`In the desktop app, a game whose page stops unexpectedly no longer leaves an empty green window: it opens again at the main menu, where Continue plays on from the last autosave, and it asks first if that keeps happening. With analytics on, what went wrong is sent to the makers: the privacy policy says what, so you are asked again`,`For the makers: a commit keeps the version named in the project's instructions up to date`,`For the makers, while the game runs from its source: the Studio is now a link for OBS, the game itself, to be played there or in a window. Which parts of the interface and which labels show, and a mouse pointer, are chosen in its Visibility; moving the camera in the game moves the view, camera points glide it from one to the next, and Record starts OBS. Presets, pictures and takes are gone`,`Visibility has tabs: choose what each label says, keep all lines on the map as strongly as you like, and hide traffic or people on foot`,`Lines in the menu always leads to the list of all lines, also with one line open`,`A line is renamed in the head of its window, as a vehicle is, or in its Settings tab`,`The card of a car can have the view follow it, as with a train or a bus`,`Pointing at where a car or a group on foot comes from or goes to shows the arrow of its trip on the map`,`A line and a station have tabs: what matters first, then its stops, cargo or who waits, settings and all the details; a line shows its result by the day on its first tab, and its warnings are set in its Settings tab, no longer a window of their own`,`The stops of a line are put in order by dragging, waypoints with them; a new waypoint goes where it fits the route best, and a waypoint on the map can be dragged to another place`,`Zooming with an analytics map on stutters far less, most of all the map of speed limits`,`An industry and a hub have tabs too: what matters and what is wrong first, then transport, the chain, cargo, buildings and all the details`,`A window keeps its top where it is when a tab changes its height, and moves up only if it would run off the screen`,`A vehicle's card has tabs: its line, warnings and main figures first, then its load, its money and all its details`,`The lists of vehicles, of the schedule and of lines look alike: the vehicle types sit up top beside the main button, the counts are gone, and lines can be searched and filtered by several types at once, in a wider Lines window`,`A town has four tabs, Overview, Needs, Transport and Trends, with a strip of figures and clearer charts; its Overview names what it wants most and what happened of late, and analytics has the picture tabs too`,`Tall windows stop a little sooner, and Finance has small picture tabs under its title, with the name of the one you are on in the title; its balance and loan figures stand on Overview only`,`A game with many buses and lorries runs smoother: the company no longer looks for the same ways again for shared vehicles that stand still`,`A game with shared vehicles or work by time of day runs far smoother: the company no longer works out which vehicle goes where again for every vehicle standing in a depot`,`For the makers: the developer tools say that their Simulation figures are per frame, not per tick`,`A Large map takes about a third less memory: the game lets go of what it no longer needs once a drawing is on the graphics card`,`The game no longer keeps taking more memory as it runs: drawings of the map that are gone leave no oversized buffers behind`,`For the makers: a run that measures what the released game keeps in memory over a long time (pnpm memory)`,`The welcome on the first start no longer says the game is free`,`What is new no longer opens by itself when a new version starts: it opens from What's new and the version in the main menu, or from the settings`,`A slip road that joins a highway at the mouth of a tunnel now ends there, instead of drawing its lane on past the tunnel, and a slip road that climbs straight from a highway to a bridge keeps its road surface`,`Cars, buses and lorries go under the ground right at the mouth of a tunnel, instead of showing on top of it for the first half of the way, and the foot of a ramp no longer throws the shadow of a bridge`,`Lorries on a yard can no longer block each other for good: where they wait on each other in a circle, the one driving out goes through, and a yard already stuck in a save frees itself`,`A big map that takes long to open, or a moment in which the game itself is held up, no longer counts as a simulation that stopped answering: no message to restart it, and no going back to the last save`,`With analytics on, the game also sends how long its longest frames took, and how the simulation stood if it stops answering, to find what still holds games up. The privacy policy says so and asks again`,`The rest of the radio that finishes downloading while you play is on the air from the next song, and a file that cannot be read or has no songs no longer takes the songs the radio already has away`]},{version:`0.7.0`,date:`2026-10-31`,changes:[`Modifying a turning loop or a bus terminal beside a road no longer offers pavement, storage and lorry stops: those are for hubs and stations`,`The radio has six more songs, with Pop as a new genre to pick`,`DJ Danny has more to say between songs, as often as before, and goes through all his lines before he says one again. The game has more of them in it, and the rest come with the radio`,`The Quarry Times: a newspaper beside the radio, with a red number for new reports. It has everything that is reported in your game, now also the first transport of a city, opens on what is new, has filters and ads from CrossCo and Flatpakk, and a click on a story takes you there. The radio tells only some of it, and the news list has left the Radio window`,`The upkeep of a shared vehicle parked in its depot is shown as Shared vehicles in service in the finance window, not as Lines that are gone`,`The demand of a stop and of a line look the same now: a bar for each hour in the colours of the schedule, and a line across where what the vehicles can carry is`,`Bus lines at turning loops: buses drive at night again when some are taken off, no bus stands for good in its bay on its way to park, and buses no longer pile up at the first stop for a round time inflated by their own queue`,`Bus terminals look better: real lanes that run on from the drives without a break, platforms that follow the turns, slimmer roofs, and beds with trees, flowers and hedges in place of rows of benches. Turning loops get hedges and the same drives`,`Buses turn in to a bus terminal or turning loop in one smooth curve and keep to its lanes, and articulated ones bend round the corners instead of swinging across the kerbs`,`No car parks at the kerb in front of a bus terminal, turning loop, vehicle depot or parking any more, and vehicle depots and parkings open into the road with a proper drive and rounded kerbs`,`Two long buses that turn opposite ways round a corner of a simple road no longer stand for ever, each waiting for the other, with their line, its way to the depot and the traffic behind them all stuck`,`The analytics of a line have a Money tab: what it made over the last two weeks and by the day, green for a gain and red for a loss`,`The game no longer freezes with "The simulation is not answering" on going back to the main menu, or on opening a save made while a town was planning: the menu is put away before a new map or a game loads, and its sounds stop then`,`The message that the simulation is not answering stays while it lasts, with buttons to restart the simulation from the last autosave or to reload the page. Where a new version of the page went up meanwhile, the game reloads instead of standing still`,`A bug report takes the logs of the game along and says exactly which build it came from, and the saved game is on by default: switch it off with its button`,`A track can branch off where a signal stands: the signal stays, for the trains that come along its own track`,`A train line with several platforms chosen at a stop is drawn to and from each of them`,`Export logs in the developer tools reaches back 30 minutes and shows how the simulation and the drawing stood every few seconds, so a game that stands still can be looked into. The window that stops the game has the button too`,`The game keeps running when you switch to another tab or put the window away: pause it first if you want time to stand still, or turn off Run in background in the Graphics window`,`A game that stands still after coming back to its tab gets going again: the map starts drawing again, and a simulation that no longer answers is started anew from the last autosave, a few seconds back. A simulation that hangs can no longer overwrite the autosave with an incomplete one`,`The radio has a song of each genre and the name of the station in the game itself, and plays them from the start. The rest of its library comes as additional content, downloaded in the background with its progress in the main menu, and kept for the next start`,`The roofs of Flatpakk, CrossCo, Pestlé and T. I. Porton carry their real logos, in the colours of each company`,`OneMoreFM, the radio: music plays while you play, with the button in the bottom left corner on the Atlas map (the top right in Paper and Night, so also in build mode, line mode and the analytics). Tick the genres you want, skip a song, set its volume. With the game paused it sounds as if from the next room, and build mode muffles it`,`Songs and the announcer fade into each other: a song fades out under the announcer and the next one fades in under the last words. The radio is a little quieter`,`Untick the genre that is playing and the radio takes a listener request: a few seconds later the song fades out under the announcer and one of the genres you kept comes on`,`Between two songs the radio has the announcer now and then, or an ad every few songs, never both at once`,`Breaking news on the radio has its own music: the song fades out, the music hits and the announcer speaks over it, then the song comes back`,`The radio dock has a Next button beside the station, and its buttons are as tall as it`,`Bus only and one-way stay as you set them while you draw roads: they no longer switch off after the first piece`,`The simple road with bus lanes, or as a bus road, has its lane lines and BUS painted on it, as the other roads do`,`Buses have sound: an engine that runs higher the faster they go, and pulling away from a stop or a light. Lorries and buses that back up beep. Industries are heard only from closer by`,`Zoomed in close to a Flatpakk or a CrossCo you hear its loudspeakers, tinny and from where it stands: offers in the day, and that it is closing soon`,`The radio reports the news of your game: a city that passes a number of people, traffic that builds up in a city, an industry that expands. Big news breaks into a song. The latest headlines are in the Radio window and kept with the game`,`The main menu has music, Old Film Ragtime by MickeysCat, from the loading screen on; it goes on as the radio when a game starts`,`Songs the radio played are kept, so it also plays without the internet`,`Every new map has the same names for its biggest cities: Quarry Bank (one of the two biggest), Havenport, Thornwick and Oldbridge, so the radio can talk about them`,`The developer tools have a Radio group: the next song, with the announcer, after an ad or a story, breaking news, and news reported for the town in view`,`The cities and the wind sound quieter and the traffic, the buses and the trains are heard from closer by: up close they stand out more than before`,`The game talks to its backend with the newer version of its library (1.8.0), which can download sets of files apart from the game, kept in the browser for the next start: ready for the radio, while all the sounds stay inside the game`,`The sounds of the game download faster: packed from 9 MB to 5 MB, the loops that are heard in one place as one track, with no change you can hear`,`The city bus, the minibus and the articulated bus have more detail: a rounded nose with the windscreen round it, mirrors, windows down both sides, ribbed bellows, and a roof tinted in the colour of the line with the air conditioning and hatches on it`,`The trains, the lorry and the long-distance bus have more detail too: passenger cars with a broad light roof, boxes of gear at each end and a skylight in the middle, gangways between them, the ends of a railcar set and the electric locomotive with a rounded nose, windscreen and mirrors, a fast locomotive with a light roof, containers ribbed on wagons and lorries, a lorry cab with a rounded nose, mirrors and a fairing on its roof, and a long-distance bus with long windows`,`Buses and lorries in bends cost less to draw: their drawing turns with them instead of being drawn again in every frame`,`With analytics on, the game sends how a game goes at the end of each game day instead of a note every minute of play: its towns, how content they are, its industries and what was carried, for balancing the game. The privacy policy says so and is asked again`,`An industry that stands on the land of a hub opens again with a click on its site, and the card of the hub lists the industries on its land: a click opens one, its pin shows it on the map`,`Graphical detail, a new graphics option, High in the desktop app (locked in the browser): the main map gets guard rails on bridges and round their corners, soft shadows under bridges, marker posts along highways, banks up to bridges and along rivers, deeper water with ripples, more trees and bushes round junctions, and stones in the ballast. It is all drawn once with the map, so it costs next to nothing more while the game runs`,`In the New map form the level of the simulation is now called Simulation detail, apart from Graphical detail in the Graphics settings`,`Traffic no longer freezes for good: two cars that pull out of parking close together no longer each wait for the other for ever, and cars no longer stand stacked on top of each other just past a junction with traffic lights. A game where that already happened moves again once loaded`,`The Analytics window of a busy stop or station no longer drops the frame rate: its day ahead is worked out much faster with shared vehicles, and kept for a moment instead of on every redraw`,`Where WebGPU fails in Firefox, the game starts again drawn with WebGL, as it already did in Chrome and Safari`,`Demolish takes more at once: a double click on a road or a track takes all of it up to the next junction either way, and a drag along roads or track takes every piece the pointer passes over`,`Turning loop (Loop in the Stop menu): a new building beside a road or on a hub. Buses drive in at its gate, round to a free stop along its platform, take people on and drive on round the loop at its far end and out at the same gate, never backing. It starts with one stop and is made longer for more, up to eight; buses that do not call there turn round in it too. Its island is green, with trees and flowers`,`Bus terminal (Terminal in the Stop menu): a block beside a road or on a hub with two to eight parallel bays that run in from the road, platforms with shelters under a roof between them. Buses come in at the gate at one end, drive nose first into a free bay, and go out at the gate at the other end. The gates of both keep clear of junctions. Its ways through are only painted on its pavement, with benches at either end and on each platform`,`When the computer cannot keep up with the speed chosen, a red warning sign stands beside the speed buttons, and pointing at it says the speed the game really runs at. Its room is kept, so the top bar no longer jumps when it comes and goes`,`The bus stops of the build bar are one button, Stop, with the stop and the bay in its menu`,`In build mode a Size hint stands beside Rotate wherever what you place can be made bigger or smaller: Ctrl and the mouse wheel`,`The developer tools can export the logs of the last minute as a text file (Export logs, also in the console): warnings and errors always, and with the developer tools on every line of the console, the commands sent and what came of them, toasts and changes of speed`,`Bus stops keep clear of junctions: a bay no longer reaches into the junction or over its crossing. One placed too near a junction moves along its road to where it fits, and its blueprint shows it there, drawn as it will stand. The pavement widens behind a bay so people keep room to walk, and a bay of an older game near a junction is drawn shorter`,`Turning a station, a depot, a yard, storage, a lorry stop, a vehicle depot, a parking or a triangle of track before you place it turns it round its middle, which stays under the pointer: before, it swung round its first track or its front and had to be moved back after every turn`,`Cars keep to the lane connections the player set at a junction also when they cannot change lane in time, and a car behind another at a light that has green for only some turns waits for its own turn`,`In the card of a junction, Copy and Paste the lane connections or the program of the lights to another junction laid out alike; Paste puts up lights where there are none`,`In the Traffic lights tab every lane coming in has its light at its start, green, red or amber where only some of its turns have green: a click switches all of them. A turn can be red in every phase, and the card warns of it`,`Changing a junction is easier to hit: a click anywhere on a lane connection chooses it and shows a cross on it, and only the cross takes it away. Select takes up the Junction tool on a junction, both zoom in on it, its own mark steps aside while it is changed, and the editing has its sounds`,`Traffic lights by turn: the card of a junction has a Lanes and a Traffic lights tab. Pick a phase in the Traffic lights tab and every turn of the junction shows on the map green or red in it; a click on a turn switches it, so a phase can be a protected left turn only. Each phase shows a small picture of its green turns instead of road numbers, and the numbers on the map are gone`,`At traffic lights what has green waits for what is still in the junction across its way, so the junction empties before the next turns go and turning cars no longer stand in the middle`,`In build mode every crossing has a mark of its own, as junctions with lights have their green one: a click on it, with Select or Junction, opens the card of the junction`,`Arrows are painted on the lanes before a junction, as on real roads: left, straight on, right or combined, as the lanes are connected there. They show on roads with two lanes or more each way, and on every road into a junction whose lanes you set`,`Junction in the road group of the build bar replaces Lights: a click on any junction opens its card with its lanes and its traffic lights. With the tool in hand the junction shows its lane connections as curves in the Lanes tab of its card: click a lane coming in, then a lane going out, to connect them, or the middle of a curve to take it away. A dedicated turn lane or a turn over two lanes is a few clicks; cars choose their lane by it and never take a turn with no connection left. Reset lanes gives the junction its own back, and traffic lights are put up from the same card`,`The ship command includes a Linux AppImage for backend updates and itch.io downloads`,`The ship command shortens the notes of a build of the app to what the backend takes, where a long version stopped it`,`The desktop app saves in the background: the autosave no longer holds up the window for a moment while it is written to disk`,`The desktop app opens where you left it, at its size, maximised or in full screen, and shows its window only once the game has drawn`,`The desktop app no longer reloads the game by Ctrl+R or F5 or zooms the page by Ctrl and plus or minus, as a browser would`,`The desktop app keeps a game that runs going at full speed with its window behind others, where a Mac slowed it down`,`A save file dropped on the window of the game plays it, as Load save file does`,`The developer tools can draw the map in a worker of its own, as a trial (Draw the map in a worker, under State): it keeps the map smooth while the windows are busy, but has no icons on the map yet`,`The car park of a station is painted on its forecourt: bay lines on the pavement, with faint tyre wear where cars drive, instead of a raised block with a strip of green. Cars turn off the road where the drive of the forecourt meets it, drive along the lane and stand in the painted bays. The cars parked on the pavement of a hub stand in painted bays too`,`People on foot walk down the middle of the pavement and never on the road or in the parking at the kerb: along the pavement as it is drawn, behind the parked cars where the parking is set into it, easing out and in where it begins and ends, round the corners of the junctions and over the zebras to cross`,`Kerbs at junctions are clean: parking strips at the kerb end in a gentle taper before the rounded corner, so the kerb line runs on into it with no bumps, stubs or double edges`,`Towns no longer end in a hard edge: along the roads out and just past the outer streets stand houses with their gardens, alone and in small groups, thinner further out, and farmsteads with a barn and a yard further off; trees, bushes and small fenced gardens with the odd shed fill the open ground round the houses and between the streets of a village, with bushes along the verges and hedges along the backs of the gardens. Most of it at Detailed, less at Standard. It is countryside: nobody of the town lives there, roads and stations clear it for free, and a town that grows there clears it too`,`The pavements of the towns are smooth and clean: they follow the rounded kerbs round every corner, run on unbroken past gardens and business plots instead of under them, and widen behind parking at the kerb so people keep room to walk. Parking at the kerb runs on past a driveway or a join in the street instead of dipping in and out. Gardens, their paths and driveways reach right up to the pavement`,`Car parks in towns fill their whole block: one paved surface with rows of bays, green islands with trees at the ends of the rows and between them, a green edge with a hedge or a fence round some, and a way in that opens into the street with rounded kerbs. The courts behind the buildings of a town centre have rounded corners and a way in from a street through a gap between the buildings, where the cars drive in and out`,`The ground of a block that is one thing reaches under its pavement, so the pavement lies on it with no gap or second edge: the grass of a car park and a park, the asphalt round a shop such as a CrossCo, and the paving of a town centre, which no longer turns to grass where a road, a stop or a station comes near. A park with open ground beside it has a hedge round it, open where its paths leave. The way into a car park or a court runs from its aisle straight into the road, its kerbs turning round into the kerb of the road, also where parking at the kerb runs past it`,`On a new map the long blocks of the towns have a footpath across them, from one street to the next between the houses, in a gentle bend: the gardens are laid out round it, and people on foot take it as a shortcut`,`One-way is now a switch at the end of the road settings, for any kind of road: a road built one-way has all the lanes of its kind going the way you draw. The One-way road is gone from the road menu; those already built stay`,`A Custom road in the road menu opens a window with a picture of the road as it will look: set the lanes forward and back (1 to 4 each, so a road can have three lanes in and one out), a bus lane on either side, the speed limit (30 to 120 km/h) and a strip down the middle. Its width and price follow, and Custom keeps what you set for next time`,`A road can no longer be built across an industry or anything of yours, nor widened over it: it shows red and says what is in the way. Houses a new or wider road takes down are shown red before you build, and are paid for and counted against their town, as for a station`,`The developer tools no longer open by themselves in the main menu: their keys open them there`,`The main menu has a badge on the logo that says which build you play: Browser, Desktop or Demo, and Development on yellow and black stripes for a build of the next version`,`What is new in a version, or a message of the makers, opens a moment after the main menu has come in, where it opened while the logo was still flying in`,`The developer console and tools open in the main menu too, on the game behind it`,`A build of the game for CrazyGames: it opens straight into a first Small map with the tutorial, saves, statistics and settings are kept with your CrazyGames account, their sound setting is followed, and it has their ads (a banner in the main menu and while a map is made, a video when a new game starts), no links out of the game and no Feedback window (pnpm crazygames, or CrazyGames in pnpm ship)`,`The main menu is drawn smaller where the window is too low for it, so its buttons stay in reach`,`Buses keep to the way of their line: one that stood at its stop just past the spot no longer drives round the block before going on`,`People on foot walk at walking pace beside the cars, so far more of them are out at a time; passengers walk to their station or stop and on from it, in small groups; at Detailed nobody made up walks up and down the streets, forecourts or paths any more: only people with somewhere to go are on foot, and the made up ones stay about gardens, courts and parks`,`Commuters go each morning to where their household works and come home in the evening, pupils to their own school: industries and industrial estates get their full share of workers, also from the towns around, and a Flatpakk draws shoppers from further. The Commuters map names each industry and estate with how many work there, and Journeys and Hot zones count the same trips`,`Cars turn through junctions smoothly: no more stutter on tight turns, no jump sideways where a car turns into a short road or leaves the curve of a junction, and no jump where a car brakes to a stop`,`Cars park at a believable pace: they crawl along the drive and the aisle of a car park, slow down into the bay, and stand a moment before they back out slowly; pulling in at the kerb is slower too, and a car waiting for a gap to pull out stands still`,`Two new maps under Analytics: Commuters, the people of each district on their way to work by car, by line or on foot, and Parking, how full every car park, garage and kerb is and how many trips found no parking in each town today`,`The maps of the analytics read what the households do: Traffic, Noise and Pollution count only the trips that drive, Journeys shows the trips by car, by line or on foot, and Hot zones every trip of the day; they are worked out off the screen, once an hour, so opening one no longer stalls the game`,`The town window shows the trips out of the town today by car, by line, on foot and dropped for no parking, with the car share, and the car share day by day under Trends: the fewer cars, the better`,`Click a car or a group of people walking to see whose they are: the household and its home, where they come from and go, why (work, school, shops, leisure or home), and where the car will park or how the group goes`,`City car parks are laid out properly: a drive in from the street, rows of bays at an even pitch with an aisle each side, no bay across the drive, and a strip of green at the far edge. Cars drive in along the drive and down the aisle to their bay`,`Cars park on the land of the buildings: in the bays behind and beside blocks of flats, offices and shops, on driveways beside some houses (with a garage at the end for some), and in garages inside houses and under bigger blocks, out of view. A car at home looks there first, then at the kerb, then in a car park; a trip into a district takes the bays of its offices and shops for half of the cars. The parked cars of scenery on those bays are gone: the cars there are the real ones`,`Home and visitor parking is spread over every street of a district: a car drives to the nearest of the few points of its district that ways are kept for, and finds the last few streets from there itself`,`No car parks at the kerb across a way in: the drive of a car park, the way down into a garage, a driveway or the way into a court; the parking strip leaves a gap there`,`People choose how they go: by train or bus as many as the lines draw, on foot when it is short, else by car. Who finds no parking where they drive takes the line instead if there is one (and keeps doing so for a while), or walks if it is not far, else stays at home: lines carry more where parking is short. People walk to and from the stations and stops`,`At Detailed the people walking from their parked cars and on short trips are on the map: each household as a group of one to five, children smaller, along the pavements, waiting at traffic lights for green; fewer made-up walkers where they are. A walk starts and ends on the pavement beside a street of its place, and goes along the pavements, the paths of parks and forecourts, crossing at junctions and on zebras, waiting on the kerb at lights; never across lots, buildings or lanes. Groups walk loosely, most people alone, children smaller, and people fade in and out one by one as you zoom and where a walk starts and ends`,`Trees are drawn over the cars and buses again, which still drive over paving and markings`,`No public garages under car parks for now: a car that stood in one, in a saved game, parks elsewhere`,`Kerb parking only in the streets of a town: none out in the country or on an industrial estate`,`Cars and buses are drawn over the paving of industries, shops and stations and the marks on it, no longer under it`,`The dark at the mouth of a tunnel deepens smoothly instead of in steps`,`Fewer jams at Detailed: a car takes the inner lane of a road of two for a turn across the other way and the outer for the other side, so those that drive on pass one that waits; one turning across that is in a junction already goes first; a ring of cars that give way breaks quicker; nobody sets out while the roads are full of standing cars; and on new maps a stub of road between a junction and a bend is made one with the road after it, so the roads empty again by night`,`Fewer jams that never drain: a car whose way out of its spot is full stays parked and tries again, one that has waited at a busy road is let in, cars no longer crowd into a junction whose exit is already taken by others in it, a car held at a full road near where it is going parks at the kerb there, a ring of cars that all give way breaks after a few seconds, and nothing turns back along a dead end to queue at the same junction again`,`A car keeps its colour from the spot it pulls out of to the spot it parks in: it no longer changes as it pulls into the lane (saves of before keep the cars that stand as they were drawn)`,`Cars at the kerb stand in a parking strip with marked bays beside the lanes, never in a lane: every street with kerb spots has its strip drawn where its cars park`,`The people of a town live in households, each with a home in a district, a place of work and school it keeps, and its cars: a household of 40 people at Standard, a real one of 2 to 5 at Detailed. Their cars stand at home in the streets of their district at night, drive to work in the morning, park there and come back to stand at home again`,`The car trips of the day are planned an hour ahead in a helper thread beside the simulation, and set out at their time: the busy hours of a town are as before`,`The kerb spots of a street that is taken away, split, or given a bus lane or a stop are free at once, and the cars that stood in them are gone, where they stood taken until their cars drove off`,`Fewer cars on the roads, each standing for more trips: one for every 40 at Standard with 450 at the most, one for every 15 at Detailed with 800, so the streets are less jammed and a town is busiest in the morning and the evening`,`Every car knows where it will park before it sets out: a spot at the kerb of a street or a spot of its own in a car park, and it drives straight there instead of circling the block. Streets have a row of kerb spots by their length (none on highways, slip roads, bus lanes or by bus stops); in town and station car parks cars now drive in to their own spot and back out, as at industries`,`Parked cars stay where they parked and are drawn standing there, and the same car drives home from that spot when the day of its people ends: commuters come home in the evening and the town empties at night`,`The developer tools can unlock the full game in a browser (Unlock the full game here), to try the detailed simulation and huge maps there`,`More coaches no longer make a passenger train slower: a long fast train runs at 160 km/h like a short one, and only takes longer to get going. A freight train keeps its speed with more wagons than before (five behind the standard locomotive), and the heavy one is the quicker from seven on and gets a long train going sooner`,`The Buy vehicle window is wider: every type in a list on the left, with a search and the vehicle kinds to filter it, and on the right the one chosen drawn large with its top speed as a sign and its figures, its parts and its work side by side, and a graph of how quickly it gets going empty and full; every part keeps its place and size as you choose`,`The window of a vehicle in Vehicles is laid out the same: drawn large with its top speed and figures, then the result of its line day by day beside its work, and is a little narrower`,`The card of a vehicle shows its line as a band in the line colour with the stop it came from and the next one, which move along as it runs, the vehicle type under the line name and its speed as a sign beside them, and the running cost beside the passengers and the last trip`,`The wheels and the diesels of a train sound quicker the faster it goes, and slow down with it as it rolls into a station`,`A full train gets going a little more slowly than an empty one, by what its passengers or goods weigh`,`The vehicle shop and the parts of a train show how many seconds it takes to reach its top speed`,`A new bus, the long-distance bus, with windows all along its sides: 100 km/h on highways and fast roads, 50 seats, slower to get going and dearer to run than a city bus`,`A new map, Speed limits: every road and stretch of track coloured by how fast it may be driven, with a speed-limit sign on it; it can be laid over the map in build mode too`,`Laying track or a road shows a speed-limit sign on it, where a curve of track is slowest and on straight track the speed of the fastest train, in place of the max km/h of the tip; the build bar shows the limit of a road as a sign`,`A town looks for ground to build on at the end of its day in a helper thread beside the simulation, one to four of them by the cores of the computer: what it finds is built five game minutes later, where nothing was built over it meanwhile, and the longest tick of the night of a big map is about a third as long; the Simulation load panel shows a row for each helper and the cores used`,`The tick bench also times the night of full towns that all look for ground, and a road taken away from a played game, with the work of the jobs apart`,`A lorry stop is sized by its bays in the bar, 2 to 12, where it had the length slider of a station; storage gets a slider from its own least length, in steps of its land`,`No containers are drawn beside the bays of a lorry stop any more: it keeps no goods`,`Traffic moves in steps of two ticks and is drawn smoothly between them: a busy map spends half the time on its cars, and the game is the same at every speed, with no simpler junctions at 40x`,`At a junction only the vehicles near enough to meet are compared with each other, and none that stands with no room: the traffic of a busy map takes about a quarter less time again, and drives exactly as before`,`A lorry on its way out of a yard waits further back behind one at the gate, so the trailer of that one no longer swings into it as it turns out`,`A lorry line that loads at the lorry stop of a cargo station what trains unload there is no longer warned that nothing brings it, and the card of the cargo station lists the lines of its lorry stops`,`Taking out planned track takes the planned signals on it with it: the plan no longer says Nothing there any more and refuses to be built`,`Adding a lorry stop or storage to a hub no longer lags while you place it: the blueprint is worked out once for each square of the hub the pointer is in, not at every move`,`A train that stands the wrong way for the waypoints of its line runs to a track end to turn round first, where it stood blocked for good; a waypoint or a stop that a train, bus or lorry cannot reach is left out and it goes on to the next (a stop only on a line of three or more)`,`A deleted line with lorries that carry goods no stop of it takes now closes: they give those goods up and park, where they stood at their stop for good and the line could not be edited or deleted`,`The button of an update of the app shows how far it has downloaded again, first, and a development build by its short name (0.6.2-dev), the full one when the pointer is on it`,`Feedback replies from the team arrive formatted, and test games played while building the game no longer count in the statistics`,`Sending the game out asks, in a menu, which branch and which build of the version to send and what to send it to, and can bump the version there too, instead of only sending the branch already checked out`,`Running the tests can be done from a menu too, picking which parts of the game and searching for a test file as you type, with live progress of each part, a summary of what passed and what failed and a look at the full report of anything that did not; sending the game out shows each of its steps live the same way`,`The simulation can be timed by itself on two played games, phase by phase and against an earlier run, to see what a change to it costs (pnpm bench)`,`A game with many buses and lorries runs much faster: which vehicle depots a line can reach is kept until the roads or stops change, and how many vehicles a line should run is counted directly where no vehicle is shared, instead of planning the whole fleet for every lorry in every tick`,`The developer tools have a Simulation load panel beside Frames a second: how busy the thread of the simulation is, how many ticks a second it makes of those the speed asks for and whether it falls behind, how long a tick takes, and a row for each thread that works for it`,`Jammed junctions cost less: a car that keeps to the way it has taken through a junction keeps what was worked out for it from one step of the traffic to the next, and a vehicle with no room left is compared with no more of the others`,`The simulation sends what changed to the screen for about half the work: a record is compared with what was last sent of it without writing it out as text, only the fields that changed go, and the company no longer goes whole with its history every tick`,`At high speed the simulation no longer stands idle between its runs of ticks: the browser made it wait 4 to 8 ms each time, up to a third of its time on a computer that could not keep up`,`Trains and lorries that wait at a stop or in a depot cost far less: whether their line wants more or fewer vehicles out is read off its schedule where that settles it, and the time of day is worked out once a tick`,`Where the computer cannot keep up with the speed chosen, the top bar shows the speed the game really runs at beside the speed buttons (40× · 14×), with a question mark that says why`,`The desktop app isolates its page from other sites (cross-origin isolation), which lets the simulation later share its memory between several threads; the web page is unchanged`,`Lorries and buses no longer jitter on the yard of an industry, a parking or a depot when the game runs faster than normal: they were drawn as far back as all the ticks of a frame twice over, and jumped forwards and back every frame`,`A one-way road in a town is no longer fenced off like a highway: it has pavement and crossings as the other streets do, and dirt tracks may run out on to it; only highways and slip roads have a fence along them`,`Where the trains, buses and lorries are, how fast they go, their timers and their wear are kept in one table, as the cars are, and sent to the screen as one block: what is sent of the vehicles each frame shrinks to their few changes`,`Parking, the cars of the households and the walks are tidied up inside, so later work on them is easier; the game plays exactly as before`,`Industrial estates look laid out: each yard and forecourt has a drive in from the street whose kerb turns round into it, with no car parked across it, and the plots at the end of a block follow the slant of its side street instead of leaving a wedge of grass. At Detailed the leftover corners of towns and estates (between plots, at block corners, beside yards and car parks) have a tree, a few bushes or a round clump of flowers here and there, and some buildings a row of flowers along a wall`]},{version:`0.6.1`,date:`2026-10-27`,changes:[`Analytics counts a shared vehicle only on the line allocated for the selected time of day, even while it still runs on another line`,`Bus lines show their red capacity line in the analytics and their capacity in the schedule before a full round is run, and count shared vehicles that run on them`,`Demolishing track that runs on out of a station or a depot marks and takes down only the free stretch outside it, and making a station bigger on a long track keeps the far ends of the track in place`,`Modify: what is added to a hub or a station has its settings in the bar again: level, length and tracks of a station, depot or yard, the length of storage and lorry stops, the bays of a vehicle depot; storage and lorry stops always stand on the ground`,`Modify of a station that is planned but not built yet: the bar shows the name and marks the tool in use (it kept Pavement marked after Storage or Lorry stop was picked); the station is made bigger once it is built`,`Placing a building on a hub in Modify no longer slows the game down: it is checked about four times faster, more so on big hubs with many buildings, and a selected hub is framed without working out all its land every frame`,`Modify of a train depot or yard no longer offers road depots and parkings, and Select in build mode no longer offers to modify a station or depot that is only planned, not yet built`]},{version:`0.6.0`,date:`2026-10-25`,changes:[`Traffic lights: put them at any junction with Lights in the road group of the build bar, and click lights (with Select of build mode too) to set their program: phases with the roads that have green, how long, the pause between phases, an offset, and links to other lights that then run the same program on the same clock`,`The roads of selected traffic lights are numbered on the map, each in the colour its light shows now; linked lights show theirs smaller, joined by green dots, and are listed in the card; the phase that runs is marked in the card, a phase pointed at shows on the map, and the selected lights keep their green mark, ringed`,`Traffic lights pause 4 seconds with red for all between phases, and a changed program runs on in the phase it was in instead of jumping; taking out the phase that runs gives red for all, then the next. Lights set at a junction that loses its roads go with them`,`In build mode every junction with traffic lights has a green mark; the Lights tool shows the lights it would put up before the click, and says when they are up. Traffic lights are selected in build mode only`,`Road building: drawn from one point of a road to another, the road between is upgraded along its way, bends and all, and the tip says Upgrade; a one-way road drawn along others turns those that run against it, and what cannot be upgraded says why`,`Road building shows the road as it will look while you draw it, small dots on the nodes of nearby roads, and guide lines straight on from open road ends; guide lines of roads and track fade out and hold the pointer only near their end`,`Bus roads: set Bus to Only in the road bar to build or rebuild a road for buses and lorries only, which cars keep off; the Bus setting is Off each time the road menu is opened`,`Bus stop bays beside a road with bus lanes are painted in the bus lane colour`,`Cars park at the kerb of one-way streets too, and never beside a bus road`,`Fewer junction gridlocks: a car drives out of an overlap at its rear, opposite lanes of a narrow road no longer block each other, and a deadlock is released only for the first car of a lane`,`Cars that stop short no longer jitter back and forth, and junction traffic takes about half the time it took to work out`,`A car that changes lane close to a junction, or changes back, glides over instead of jumping sideways`,`Articulated buses bend smoothly round corners, junctions and depot yards and never jump between them; their tail and brake lights stay on their back half`,`Buses back into the bays of depots and parkings and drive out forwards, as lorries do at loading bays`,`Buses and lorries waiting for a free bay queue in their lane behind each other instead of standing on the verge; buses steer into stop bays instead of sliding`,`Cars no longer vanish from a jam: one held outside a full junction turns round or takes another road where it stands, and a vehicle released from a deadlock drives on instead of crawling`,`Queued long vehicles keep one rear-footprint record per connector, preventing repeated occupancy growth on short links`,`Cars prepare their turn lane before junctions; one leading vehicle may edge through a long standstill to clear a deadlock`,`Vehicles already inside a junction finish clearing when the lights change; light-controlled queues keep waiting at their stop line`,`Vehicles can choose a free exit lane before entering a junction; parked cars wait for a gap, and long-waiting turns get room to clear`,`Junction queues wait outside until their exit has room and recover from old gridlocks; at 40× speed junction conflicts are simplified while lane paths, lights and road queues remain`,`Cars, buses and lorries follow lane paths through junctions, give way according to lights and road priority, and block crossing traffic until their whole body clears; developer traffic overlays show these paths and occupied space`,`Cargo station cards now include added storage in their capacity and cargo totals; Storage has a stacked-container icon`,`The developer menu shows whether the simulation worker is starting, running, paused, unresponsive or failed`,`Remove paved areas from stations and hubs in Modify by drawing their corners; pavement supporting buildings and vehicle approaches is protected`,`Add paved areas to existing passenger and cargo stations from Modify, using the same pavement tool as hubs`,`Smoother at the high speeds: vehicles glide evenly between the moments the simulation sends, where before they stood still for most of a frame and then jumped ahead, by more or fewer steps each time, and trains and cars no longer move out of step with each other`,`The map-generation progress card no longer shows the map size and seed`,`At startup ONE MORE appears first, then ROUTE slides down from behind it before the menu starts loading`,`The loading logo moves into its place in the main menu as the map fades into view and the menu cards arrive`,`The green logo badge has a solid lower outline without a transparent seam`,`The line in the OneMoreRoute logo fills smoothly in small increments as the game loads. It stays full for half a second and appears again when returning to the main menu`,`TransportIt! is now OneMoreRoute, with a new logo and Reddit community. The balance takes the place of the name in the game header; existing saves and settings still work`,`Cars on the roads take less work: on a big map with many cars a tick of the game is about a third quicker, and leaves the browser less memory to clear away`,`The simulation runs in a thread of its own, beside the drawing of the map: the map stays smooth while the game works out what happens, at every speed, and saving no longer holds the game up for a moment. If the simulation ever fails, the game stops with a window that says so, its last save kept`,`A save with a car whose numbers are out of range loads with them put right, and cars drawn after another game is loaded no longer take on how those of the game before were drawn`,`The game stands while its tab or window is out of sight, as it did before, and a bug report sent after the game stopped still comes with its save`,`Smoother while the towns build: a new street of a town opens on the full hour, together with all else that is done by then, so the cars find their ways over it once. Before, every street opened at a moment of its own and each was a jerk, on a big map a tenth of a second and more`,`Smoother zooming: the signals, the lines, the map of the analytics and the room the names take are drawn again as the zoom passes a step, not in every frame of a zoom, and the works under way are no longer all drawn again while the view moves`,`Laying track, a signal or a depot no longer has every car on the roads find its way again, nor do people moving in or out of a town at night; and building anything, a bus stop too, no longer works out every junction of the map again in one frame`,`For the makers, while the game runs from its source: a Studio in the developer tools, a window of its own, for pictures and videos of the game. A preset keeps a save, a size in pixels, a theme, what shows (names, vehicle labels, wind, the light) and a camera, whose points can follow a train or a bus; a picture can be drawn at several times, the game run on from its save to each, and Render all pictures draws them all again. A take glides along points of the camera in a recording view of the map alone, for OBS, which the Studio can start and stop recording`,`While the view follows a vehicle, its frame, the line it runs and the arrow to where it is heading are no longer drawn`,`Fewer short stops of the game on a played map: only the trains in view are drawn, which leaves the browser less memory to clear away`,`Only what is in view is drawn: the ground, the roads, the car parks, the buildings, the cars at the kerb and the lit windows were drawn whole in every frame, wherever the view was. From a town or a street a big map is half as much to draw, and the developer tools count only what is drawn`,`Shorter stops when the browser clears memory: what the map is drawn from lets go of what it no longer needs once it is drawn, which on a big map is hundreds of thousands of small things less to go through, and a paused game no longer draws its vehicles and works again in every frame`,`Fewer jerks when the browser clears memory while trains, buses and lorries run: each vehicle is drawn once and then only moved, where before all of them were drawn anew in every frame. On a played map the jerk comes about half as often. The warning signs over vehicles and the cars in the car parks are kept the same way, and an articulated bus shows its colour under its roof again`,`In the developer tools the headings Simulation, Frame and Memory have a small line of the last frames beside their figure, open or closed`]},{version:`0.5.9`,date:`2026-10-24`,changes:[`A developer console, opened and closed with the key under Escape (another can be chosen in the Keys window): type what the developer tools can do by its name, with the names that fit offered as you type, Tab to complete and the arrows to choose. It opens the developer tools and their tabs, runs their commands and switches their overlays; the settings no longer have a button for the tools`,`New map is no longer in the settings of a game: a new map is made with New game in the main menu`,`The settings of a game have a Game settings window, with the difficulty, the map seed and a button to make the money of the game unlimited, which forgives its loan and cannot be switched back`,`Versions and Privacy stand at the bottom of the settings`,`The New map form is wider, with a preview of the map beside its sliders: the land of the seed, its water and forest, and where its towns stand, drawn again as you change them. How the game is played and its seed are under them`,`The size of a map is a slider, from Small to Huge. Huge is new, nearly twice the ground of Large, and only in the desktop app, as the detailed simulation is`,`While a map is made, a card at the foot of the screen shows how far it has come, the step it is at and all the steps in a row, with a tip from the wiki to read meanwhile`,`The main menu no longer has the notice of the vehicle overview, and shows every message of the makers one under the other, the column scrolling where they do not fit the screen`,`The words of every button stand in its middle, level with its icon, and Defaults and Create map of the New map form stand at its foot`,`Trains no longer take a depot or a yard with track at both ends as a short cut, where it let them overtake a train waiting on the main line: they run through one only where there is no other way`,`A town that has built its lots again more densely shows a building on each of them: the centre of a grown town no longer stands empty, plots without houses, where it had grown the most`,`Smoother again on a big map that has been played a while: placing a station no longer costs a frame rate while the pointer rests, and costs half as much as it moves; the game itself runs about twice as fast with many trains and buses`]},{version:`0.5.8`,date:`2026-10-24`,changes:[`Editions: the game in the browser is free, and the app is the full game. The new detailed simulation is in the full game, shown with a lock in the browser, and a game made with it opens only in the full game; every size of map, Large too, is in both`,`A new map has a level of detail, Standard or Detailed, chosen in the New map form and kept with the game. In a detailed game there are more cars on the roads, each standing for fewer trips`,`Cars, buses and lorries ease into a stop they see coming, at a red light, at the back of a queue or before a turn, and brake hard only when they have to. Behind another they keep to its speed, and a queue at a light pulls away one after another rather than all at once`,`With the map near, cars blink on the side they turn to as they come to a junction, and their brake lights show by day too`,`A cargo station serves the industries within 100 m of any of its tracks, not only its first, so one made bigger keeps serving all it did; the ring of its reach while you place it goes round all its tracks`,`Roads meet more cleanly: a narrower road that runs on as a wider one through a junction widens out to it smoothly before the junction, roads with bus lanes are drawn at their full width, bus lanes end at the stop line or where the junction begins, and the parking strips at the kerb no longer overlap or poke out at bends`,`A parking is only as deep as its bays need, 20 m, and a parking or a vehicle depot beside a road stands along a straight stretch of it, clear of junctions and corners: placed too near one it moves along the road until it is clear, and where there is no room for it it is refused`,`A parking or a vehicle depot beside a wide road, as a multi-lane road with bus lanes, begins at the edge of the road instead of standing on it, with its drive across the footway`,`Placing a station near a long stretch of track, or a vehicle depot on a hub beside the line, no longer slows the game to a few frames a second`,`A short road that meets another, as the drive of a vehicle depot or the first few metres of a road that bends on, opens at the edge of the road it meets, round sharp corners, instead of reaching into its middle in spikes`,`A street that bends at a corner is drawn round a tighter curve, so that its edges follow the corners of the pavement beside it`,`A one-way road that meets a road at a steep angle meets it round a rounded corner, as any road does, instead of running into it in a sharp point as a slip road; only one that comes in at a flat angle merges`,`The developer tools have an Overlays tab: the lanes of the roads and the turns between them, the pathfinding of cars, buses and lorries in their lanes, the search of one vehicle, how much is drawn where, the plots of the towns and their room to grow, figures beside towns, stops and industries, and small panels for the frames a second and the viewport. They stay on, the window open or not, until switched off`,`A vehicle depot built on part of the pavement in front of a station takes that ground: the pavement of the station stops at its edge, and the hedges, trees, lamps and benches of the station keep off it`]},{version:`0.5.7`,date:`2026-10-23`,changes:[`Any road can have bus lanes: switch Bus lane on in the build bar, and draw along a street to give it them or take them away. Cars and lorries of nobody keep out of them, so your buses and the lorries of your lines drive past the queues. And a one-way road with two lanes`,`One-way roads and slip roads have arrows painted on their lanes, bus lanes are coloured with BUS on them, a road that gives way to the one it meets ends in a broken line with small teeth, and the zebra crossing stands back behind it`,`Where a slip road joins or leaves a highway the edge of the highway is a broken line across it, and the lines of the slip road meet it in a point`,`Junctions are drawn one way everywhere: every road opens into the junction at the same place for its surface, its lines and its bus lanes, with a rounded kerb round each corner, an eased edge where a road runs on wider or narrower or at an angle, and a slip road that follows its own edge until it is clear of the highway`,`A bus bay eases out of the road and back in, and every stop has a box painted where the bus stands, with BUS in it`,`Roads that part at a sharp angle meet in a hatched gore: the lines of the road that leaves stop short of the other, at a give way where its edge is clear, and a few trees stand on the ground between the two beyond its nose. The road that goes straight on through a junction keeps that role though another of its kind comes in at an angle, and its lines are broken across where others come in`,`A road that only bends is drawn as one road round a curve, its lines and bus lanes with it; two different roads that run on into each other, as a road into a multi-lane road or a highway into a road, are drawn as one, the one easing into the other and its lines running on into the like lines of the other; the outside of a corner too sharp for that is rounded off round the node`,`A slip road onto or off a highway parts from it in a hatched gore and has a lane of its own beside it for 60 m, which then narrows away, with a broken line between it and the highway; cars drive along that lane and move over as it narrows`,`A bus lane that begins or ends on a road without one narrows in as a wedge in its colour, with a broken line along it; bus lanes go on into a junction up to where the road beside them begins, and their BUS is spread evenly, clear of the ends`,`A bus bay, its painted box, its pad and its shelter follow the road as it bends, and the bay is one surface with the road; the strips of cars parked at the kerb ease out of the road and back in`,`At traffic lights every road stops at a line where it is clear of the roads it crosses, a sharp angle too, and its lamps stand there: cars stop at the same place`,`A road drawn straight from junction to junction over one that bends between them rebuilds that road as the new kind, rather than laying a second road across it`,`In build mode the curves of track are no longer filled with orange where a freight station stands on pavement somewhere on the map`,`Track is a menu now. Track lays up to four tracks side by side at once, chosen under Tracks, with a dot at the end of each. Crossover and Scissors join two tracks side by side where you point between them, in a bend too, and Triangle branches off a straight track or stands on its own with open ends, with one to four tracks and a radius of your choice, turned with R or Shift and the wheel`,`The houses and buildings of towns stand further back from their streets, by how wide the street is, with longer front gardens and wider pavement in the centres: a bus lane, a street made multi-lane or a bus bay no longer takes down the houses along it`]},{version:`0.5.6`,date:`2026-10-21`,changes:`The wiki is brought up to date with hubs, Modify, Storage, Lorry stops and the other changes of this version, and its entries are shorter and plainer. Stations and depots lists the stations for freight, and Signals says why a train sometimes reserves more than one block(Upgrade is now called Modify, and is the one way to change what is built: Modify on its card, or a click on it with Select, opens it with its handles. The station, depot and vehicle depot tools only build, and a bus stop is made a bay with Make bus bay on its card(Build mode always opens with Select(A station or a bus stop that a line calls at can always be demolished: another building of the same place takes over its calls, or else the line loses that stop and its panel says when it has fewer than two stops. Only a station a train stands at is kept(Lorry stops have a lorry icon in the build bar, the Modify bar and on cards, and the cargo station is called Cargo in the bars(The lorries at an industry drive over a lane and a row of bays laid out by the simulation, as at a lorry stop, and the time a call takes goes by how far away their own bay is(The pavement you lay and the pavement a place lays by itself keep to the same rules about roads, track and water(Land costs what it does by the town whose region it lies in(A hub is a turning spot only where the turn has room on its pavement, clear of what stands there(Buses and lorries come into and leave a hub by the quietest road near it: a busy road or a multi-lane one only where it is much nearer, and never a highway(What is selected, pointed at or being placed is framed by exactly the ground it takes, in build mode as planned and while it is dragged bigger(Storage, a lorry stop and a vehicle depot on a hub have to stand wholly on its pavement, and are refused over a road; nothing added to a hub takes down a road or a house(Track and roads can no longer be laid across a building, only across pavement(The ways vehicles take across a hub never cut through a building, their own depot neither; a parking can be driven into from either side(Storage, a lorry stop or a vehicle depot of a hub made bigger past the edge of its pavement paves the new ground with it, for the price of the land and the paving, unless something stands in the way(Nothing can be built on the land of a hub or a place outside its Modify mode: it says to modify the hub instead(In build mode what is planned or being placed has a fine outline, blue where it can be built and red with the overlap shaded where it lies on another building or cannot be built, and a small plate with what it is(In build mode the ground round each building that vehicles cannot drive over is hatched faintly; the row in front of the bays stays clear(In build mode a green and a red pill show where vehicles enter and leave each place, and a grey pill which way a building being placed faces(A free-standing lorry stop has a loading ramp along the back of its bays, sloping down at both ends, and takes only that ground: no empty strip behind it(Yards have a way in and a way out side by side, and several lorries and buses drive on a yard at once instead of queuing on the road while one moves(A hub with room for it is a loop to turn round through, forwards all the way; elsewhere the turn in three is sized to the vehicle, so a lorry with its trailer gets fully off the road(A trailer follows the path of its lorry round corners, on the road, at the gates and on the yard, forwards and backwards(In a vehicle depot or a parking on a hub a vehicle drives into its bay forwards and backs out where there is room, and leaves one tidy track(The drives across the sites of the industries are wider, with room for a lorry each way(A vehicle leaving a bay near the gate of a vehicle depot beside a road no longer jumps on to the road(All the pavement of a hub, a station and its yard is one surface with one kerb and one fence: the yard of a cargo station, the ground and drive of a lorry stop, vehicle depots, forecourts and depot courts are paved as part of it, with no grass gaps or fences between the pieces(Pavement reaches out to a road that runs close by, also one built later, so the two meet(The pavement of a station for passengers is dressed as a place for people, not a yard: small warm street lamps along its edge and beside the road instead of floodlights, benches, bins and planters, no fence round it, and a hedge along some of its outer sides(Storage and lorry stops have no lamp masts standing among their bays and zones any more: the floodlights of the pavement light them; those of a cargo station stand at its outer edge(A hub beside a road is a turning spot: a bus or a lorry that would have to drive on to find a way round turns through the hub instead, forwards in and backwards out, which leaves its tracks there(The way into the yard of a building on a hub is from whichever road near it leads there soonest, also a road built later(A lorry that turns out of a yard drives away once it is on the road, and is not kept waiting by the cars it held up; one may drive in while another drives out(Buses and lorries take street corners on a wider, smoother curve, and the corners of the ways on yards are rounded wider where there is room(The pavement of the company is dressed: floodlight masts along its edges that shine soft white light in over it at night, and out in the middle of wide open pavement, bins, crates, a skip or a hut beside its buildings and vans parked along its edges, never on its drives, tracks or bays; storage no longer has pallets and crates on it(A hub serves every industry near any of its land: one joined to an industry fills its storage with what the industry makes when a line loads that cargo at any of its lorry stops or stations(Storage and the yard of a cargo station are one hatched area each, its paint faded in places and kept clear of the crane rail, with one container drawn for every 10 t that lies there, stacked up to three high(The bays of a lorry stop, on a hub too, lie on the same pale concrete as those of an industry, so they stand out from the pavement(In line mode, a click on a hub adds the lorry stop or station of it that is clicked, which also gives a new line its mode(A lorry stop or station of a hub that a line calls at can be demolished when another of the hub can take over: the line calls there instead(Track over pavement of the company is set into it as at a level crossing, with no sleepers, and a yellow line painted either side(A passenger station is paved only on the side of its forecourt, out from its first platform: its tracks keep their own ground(Track drawn beside other track a few metres from where it starts no longer fails with "Too short": a piece too short to build is joined to the one beside it(A vehicle depot, a parking or a lorry stop on a hub that vehicles could not reach over its pavement gets a drive paved to it, from the road or round what walls it off, priced with what is built(The land shown in the build mode of a place has straight edges, not steps(Buses and lorries drive into a vehicle depot or a parking, back into a free bay of their own and drive out forwards, as lorries do at a dock; on a hub they come over its pavement by a way round what stands there(The ways vehicles take across the yards of lorry stops, vehicle depots and parkings are laid out by the simulation, which times their calls by them, and their tyres leave faint tracks along them, uneven and wider and darker where vehicles turn(A vehicle that turns off the road into a yard or out of one on to it, backs into a depot from the road, or pulls over, and a car that pulls in at the kerb or out of a parking, holds up the traffic behind it(A vehicle depot or a parking on a hub has to stand wholly on its pavement, and it, Storage and a Lorry stop take no land beyond the pavement(Pavement drawn over a road, track or water goes under it instead of being refused: only the squares they lie on are left out(Storage and a Lorry stop take only the ground they are drawn with, so nothing beyond it is taken down for them, and on a hub they stop before a road as anything placed does elsewhere(A selected hub, or a station with buildings added to it, is framed round all of it with a calm outline, not the steps of its land(In the build mode of a place, Select picks the building to make bigger: it is framed, and so is the one under the pointer(Ctrl and the mouse wheel make what is about to be placed longer or shorter: a station or a depot by 20 m, a lorry stop by a bay, a vehicle depot by a bay(A lorry stop is placed with 3 bays(What is planned and what is about to be placed is drawn as it will look in the plan view, with its tracks, crane, bays and numbers, in place of a plain block(The bar of a hub or a building being upgraded has the same groups as the build bar: Rail, Road vehicles and Logistics(A cargo station joins its industry with a straight band out of its side, so the fence runs on from the station and no longer reaches past the industry(When an industry is done, only the cargo stations that serve it are joined to it, not every one on the map(Towns no longer build houses on the pavement of a hub or of a place(After adding something to a hub, the build bar goes back to the tool you had, and the Rotate button names your own key for turning(Track, a road or a station in the way of Storage or a Lorry stop names it, where it said a logistics hub was in the way(A hub of your own is opened after its pavement is laid whatever its shape, and the rows of its buildings on its card point at them on the map(Cargo stations join their industries with full-width pavement and angled sides, without fences between them; existing saves gain the wider joins too(Freight buildings are called Cargo stations, including automatic names in older saves; player-chosen names are kept(Cargo stations use the same gantry crane as freight stations in hubs, with yellow hatched storage zones in every theme(Cargo stations serve industries within 100 m instead of 150 m, with visible pavement connections to each industry on any side, using the same pavement as the rest of the compound; older saves gain these links too(Rail cargo stations have no built-in lorry bays and keep one full standard freight train per track, currently 40 tonnes of each cargo; add Storage to keep more(Storage, lorry stops and freight stations on compound pavement no longer draw another pad over it in Paper and Night(Building and upgrading use the same rules for adding tracks, including stations and hubs from older saves(Upgrades under the ground keep their level in the preview and no longer charge for houses above; houses overlapping an upgrade on the ground are counted too(Every station, depot, yard, bus depot and parking stands on land of the company, which it is given as it is built and which grows with it; build mode shows its edge(Land of the company has a fence round it, open where track, a drive or a forecourt meets it(A depot or a yard has hard standing beside it, with places for cars and a drive to the nearest road(Saves of before are given the land of what stands in them(Land is bought with what stands on it: cheap in the country, dearer near a town and ten times as dear in the middle of one; the price at the pointer says how much of it is land, and the books have it as Land(The wiki says what land is and what it costs, under Building(Build mode draws stations, depots, yards and trains as a fine plan: track as two rails on sleepers, platforms with their edges, roofs and benches, the building with its door, and slim trains(Upgrade on the card of a station, a depot, a yard, a vehicle depot or a parking opens build mode on it: the view goes to it and all else is dimmed(In it, round handles at its ends make it longer as they are dragged, and handles at its sides give it a platform more at a time; a vehicle depot gets more bays by its ends(The bar of an upgrade has − and + for its tracks, its length and its bays, and what is changed is one step of the plan, priced with its land and the houses in the way(Build mode opens with Select: a click on a station, a depot or a vehicle depot opens it to be upgraded(The wiki says how upgrading works, under Building(The forecourt of a station runs its whole length, and its way past the front has a drive out to the road at either end where one is near(A bus stop near a station has a paved path to its forecourt(Buildings can be added to a place in its build mode: a station, a yard for goods, a depot, a yard, a vehicle depot or a parking, square to its ground; what stands on one place is one stop to change at, and its yards for goods keep what they hold as one(Pavement is laid in the build mode of a place by clicking its corners, which go on to the edge of a road and square to the side before(Hub in the build bar begins a logistics hub of your own with its pavement, and opens it to add its storage with loading bays, its stations and its depots(Pavement is fenced round, and a yard for goods on it has no fence of its own(Land, pavement and their fences follow straight edges: the pieces of pavement as they were laid and the ground of each building, not squares(The bar of an upgrade is one row: its name, what can be added where it is a hub, and Exit; tracks, length and bays are changed by the handles alone(A hub of your own is built from Storage, which only keeps goods and is made longer by its handles, and Lorry stops, where lorries load and unload and nothing is kept(A vehicle depot or a parking on the pavement of a hub stands anywhere on it, turned as you like, and needs no road beside it(A hub serves the industries near it, as an industrial station does(In line mode a hub is one point: a click anywhere on it adds it, and the line calls at the building of it that its vehicles use, the lorry stop for lorries and the station for trains(In build mode Select opens a hub as one, wherever it is clicked; in its upgrade a click on one of its buildings gives that one its handles(What is added to a hub turns as anything placed in build mode, from square to its pavement: R by 15 degrees, Shift and the mouse wheel by 5, and a Rotate button in the bar(A hub is one place: one sign and one card with what lies in all its yards, its lines and its buildings, which are named after it; a click on its land opens it(Fences round the land of the company never stand on pavement, only round it, and a vehicle depot has land enough for the pavement round its yard(A station with something built on to it is one place, as a hub is: one sign, one thing to select with the card of the station and its buildings, and one stop in line mode(A place is paved by itself under all that stands on it and across the ground between, where no road or other track is in the way; the pavement grows with what is added or made bigger(A station on the ground is paved out to a road that runs along a side of it within 80 m, all along, with trees on it until something is built there, in place of the drives of its forecourt; never over a town, its estate or an industry(What stands on the pavement of a place draws only its markings and its building on it, with no paving, kerb or gravel of its own(What a place paves by itself costs only its land(Cargo stations add separate Storage and Lorry stops; passenger stations have no add-on buildings for now(A lorry stop is built with two bays and gets one more for every 4 m it is made longer, up to twelve(Storage can be made up to 60 m wider by the handles at its sides, either way, and holds the more(The loading bays of a lorry stop and of a yard for goods are painted as those of an industry, with their numbers, and storage as zones hatched in yellow: one look for all of them(Storage and a lorry stop have no cabin of their own: nothing stands over their bays and zones(What is placed or made bigger shows what it will be while it is: the numbered bays of a lorry stop, the zones of storage, the bays and the shed of a vehicle depot or a parking, to line it up by(A vehicle depot or a parking is made bigger at the end that is dragged only, and no longer both ways from its middle(A vehicle depot on the pavement of a place no longer has a pad of its own drawn under it, which showed on new buildings until the game was loaded again(Pavement is closed by a click on its first corner, which shows a tick once there are three, and a right click takes back the last corner(The bar of the build mode of a place is made as the build bar is, with the same Exit, and has Demolish, which takes down a building of that place only(The lines painted on a yard for goods run its whole length, and no longer stop at its middle(Saves of before are paved as they would be built now, for nothing(The trees and the lit windows no longer vanish from the map at midnight, or when a town builds an industry(A bus or lorry standing in a parking is said to be parked there, not in for a service: only a vehicle depot services(Buses and lorries on a level crossing are drawn over the track, as cars are(A line's depot can be chosen again: pick it under Depot at the top of Edit vehicles, or Nearest. New vehicles of the line start there and go there for a service(No building can be placed on another any more, whatever kinds they are: a vehicle depot or a parking on Storage or a Lorry stop, Storage on a vehicle depot, a station grown over one. What build mode shows in red is refused(The card of Storage and of a Lorry stop has Modify, and no longer shows Tracks; Storage, which no line calls at, shows no Lines or Loading bays(Demolishing Storage or a Lorry stop costs its share of what it cost to build, as for a station, made longer and wider included`.split(`(`)},{version:`0.5.5`,date:`2026-10-19`,changes:[`The Visibility window can hide what is under the ground: tunnels, stations, depots and bus stops there, their signals and what drives in them; in build mode it always shows`,`Stairs on the pavements lead down to a station under the ground, where a pavement runs over it, but never on a car park`,`A bus that comes to a bay where another stands waits in its lane behind it, and pulls in once that one has gone, instead of standing on top of it`,`A bus that pulls out of a bay is no longer held up by the bus that waits behind it`,`A bus or a lorry held up in a queue no longer turns round in the street or at a junction to go another way: it turns only at a dead end`,`News that the makers write for players shows at the right of the main menu, and news that is to pop up opens once as the main menu is shown`,`The privacy policy says that the game asks for that news, with nothing that says who plays`,`A new map no longer stops being made where a winding road crosses a highway`,`The icons on the map show again on older versions of Chrome`,`Where Safari cannot draw a big map with WebGPU, the game starts again drawn with WebGL instead of stopping`,`A freight train or lorry that carries goods every stop of its line is too full to take shows No room to unload, with the stop, so a stuck chain is seen`,`A lorry or freight train taken off its schedule, sent to park or whose line is deleted sets down what it can and leaves what there is no room for, instead of driving round with it for ever and costing money`,`A vehicle to be sold that stands in its depot is sold at once, even with goods aboard`]},{version:`0.5.4`,date:`2026-10-19`,changes:[`Buses and lorries never turn round in a street or a junction: they drive round a block, and turn only at a dead end where there is none`,`A bus no longer turns on the spot at a stop with no way on, nor where it stood with no way`,`The wiki says how a bus turns round, under Buses`,`The game no longer slows to a crawl while the pointer is over the map of a game with many buses and lorries`,`The list of vehicles opens and updates faster with many buses and lorries`,`Where the graphics card cannot keep up, the map is drawn with fewer pixels by itself for a while, and sharp again once it can`,`Lorries at a dock cost the game a little less time`]},{version:`0.5.3`,date:`2026-10-19`,changes:[`Demolish takes a road beside a station or depot, and marks what it takes by its outline, not a circle`,`Trains and lorries load and unload again at a stop that comes twice in a row on their line`,`A train fits a platform or depot shown as long as it, though it is a little longer`,`A bus drives on from its stop and finds its way round, instead of turning on the spot`,`Where a bus or lorry must turn round, it makes a real U-turn across the road, and the traffic waits for it`,`A lorry with nothing to do at a dock no longer waits before its gate for ever, and a worn one goes for its service`,`What is new opens by itself the first time a version is played, in place of the list beside the main menu`,`What's new on the main menu, and a click on the version under its card, show it again`,`What is new shows the notes of each version as they were written for players, where there are some`,`What is new shows one version at a time, with the older ones in a dropdown, and sorts the changes into new, improved, fixed and the rest`,`What is new waits for the notes written for players, and shows its own list only when they cannot be reached`,`The rating on itch.io stands at the right of the main menu`,`Car parks, the analytics and the drawing of the map cost a little less time`,`The app for the Mac is packed again when its signature fails, and never sent out without Apple's check`,`The game talks to its backend with version 1.7.0 of its library`]},{version:`0.5.2`,date:`2026-10-18`,changes:[`Clicking an industry where your own lorries call no longer stops the game`,`A line has Settings, where its warnings can be switched off or come later, and new ones switched on`,`The Vehicles window shows what is wrong with a vehicle, and is wider`,`The panels of lines and vehicles are tidier, and deleting a line asks first`,`Following a vehicle is smooth, and its warning sign stands above its label`,`Stations, hubs and depots of the longest length can be built at an angle`,`A station or depot is clicked on its own ground, so what stands beside it can be clicked too`,`Vehicle depots and parkings can no longer be built over another road or over track`]},{version:`0.5.1`,date:`2026-10-17`,changes:[`A small update to test the updates of the desktop app`]},{version:`0.5.0`,date:`2026-10-17`,changes:[`Escape leaves the analytics`,`The price at the pointer stays beside it at every interface size`,`The keys move the map again after a slider of the build bar is used`,`A new line opens at once while a plan waits to be built`,`Vehicle depots and parkings stand as close as their sites allow, and can no longer grow onto each other`,`The schedule overview is a calendar, a row a line, with a search and filters`,`Edit schedule opens the schedule overview for the line`,`Vehicles can be searched`,`The map seed can be copied in the settings`,`A bus stop can be made a bus bay from its card, keeping its name and lines`,`Selling a vehicle twice by a quick double click no longer shows an error`,`A Visibility window, by the eye in the bottom right corner, chooses which labels the map shows and from how far`,`Vehicles have labels in the colour of their line; a line that is shown labels all of its vehicles`,`Industries are named on a plate with the icon of what they make`,`Labels fade out as the map is zoomed out, rather than vanishing at once`,`A line that is shown no longer hides the vehicles on it`,`The desktop app updates itself and offers the update in the main menu`]},{version:`0.4.9`,date:`2026-10-16`,changes:[`Choose how long vehicles wait at each stop: until full, for a while, or until unloaded`,`Stations, stops, depots and vehicles can be renamed in the head of their card`,`A new line can be named at once`,`A selected vehicle shows its line on the map, with an arrow to where it is heading`,`Collieries dig three times the coal, enough for one at its top level to feed two power stations`,`Building track, roads and stations no longer stops the game for a moment`,`Buying a train no longer freezes the game on a big railway`,`Time lapse stays smooth on slower computers: the game runs as fast as the computer can`,`Vehicles that run no line are dark grey`,`A line can have a single stop or call at the same stop twice in a row; its vehicles wait until it is extended`,`Changing track while a train is on its way no longer stops the game with an error`,`Freight trains and lorries deliver their load before the schedule parks them, and loaded ones in a depot go out to deliver it`,`Vehicles park and are serviced at the nearest place from where they leave their line, their home depot a little preferred`,`Vehicles on their way to park no longer warn that there is no parking`,`Done items on the roadmap are folded away until opened`,`An idea can carry your name and a private email too, and the game remembers your name`,`Setting a waypoint in line mode no longer stops the game with an error`,`When the browser runs out of memory the game stops and offers a reload, instead of failing frame after frame`,`A works with little in its yard no longer stops the game with an error`,`A new map starts when the browser storage is full, and the game says when it cannot be saved`,`Where WebGPU fails on a graphics card, the game starts again with WebGL and keeps to it`,`A train taken off its line while it waits for new parts goes to a depot instead of blocking the line`,`Trains and buses sold on their way to a service let their passengers off and are sold in the depot`]},{version:`0.4.8`,date:`2026-10-15`,changes:`Management in the toolbox groups Vehicles, Schedule, and Finance.Company fleet and schedule overview: vehicles are shared or dedicated to a line, and can work by time of day.One Buy window for every vehicle, with a picture of each as it looks on the map.Every train is built from locomotives and wagons, and can change them later at a depot.Schedules with + and − buttons, the same in a line and in the overview, filled as far as the line is full.Articulated buses bend in the middle.Parkings for buses and lorries: on a break they wait there, and only a vehicle depot services them.Make a bus stop a bay, and a vehicle depot or parking bigger, with a click on it.Every vehicle has a home depot for its services: the nearest, or one you choose.Parked trains, buses and lorries turn their lights off.The Vehicles and Schedule overview windows no longer make the game stutter.A rail yard with more tracks than a depot can be made longer again.Freight trains run behind diesels, and fast passenger trains have a pointed nose.Freight trains and lorries are heard by their diesel engines.The cranes of the yards are heard while they load and unload a train.Locomotives for each kind of train: standard and heavy for freight, standard and fast for passengers.More wagons make a train slower; the heavy locomotive keeps its speed with long freight trains.Each locomotive looks its own: two diesels for freight, a plain and a pointed one for passengers.Trains of older saves are given standard locomotives and wagons.Lorries are quieter, and their engines sound higher the faster they drive.Chainsaws are heard at the sawmills while they have logs to cut.The Buy window no longer jumps when a warning shows.Lorries that wait for a bay stand in a line beside the road.Industries get more loading bays as they grow, where their yard has room.Sell vehicles in Vehicles, for half of what they are worth.Lines use the nearest depot: no depot to choose any more.Drag along track to place signals every so many metres.Underground stations leave the houses above, and towns build over tunnels.Settings → Keys: choose your own keys for the buttons and the analytics maps.On a tablet, pinch with two fingers to zoom.Track in line with an open end keeps the level you chose.Logistics hubs without track can no longer stand on track or on each other`.split(`.`)},{version:`0.4.7`,date:`2026-10-15`,changes:[`Optional analytics include FPS, play source, hours and player statistics`,`Feedback: private conversations and replies to the team`,`Your submitted feedback stays visible with its status and date`,`Optional name and private email when sending feedback`,`New lines show under every line filter`,`Windows show a scrollbar whenever there is more below`,`Suggest roadmap ideas and vote for planned features`,`Analytics go to our own server: the privacy policy asks once more`]},{version:`0.4.6`,date:`2026-10-14`,changes:[`Drawn with WebGPU where the browser has it: faster on big maps`,`Graphics: choose WebGL or WebGPU, and smooth edges on or off`,`Tips on the main menu when the map has lines across it`]},{version:`0.4.5`,date:`2026-10-14`,changes:[`Bigger maps with a wider border`,`New maps are made faster`,`A welcome on the first start, with the privacy policy`,`Anonymous analytics if you agree, to be switched off under Privacy`,`Yards for goods are paved and fenced in with the industry they serve`,`Painted lines and a store of pallets and crates in the yards`,`Stations, depots and yards cannot be placed on an industry`]},{version:`0.4.4`,date:`2026-10-14`,changes:[`Waypoints: click track or a road while editing the stops of a line, and its trains or buses pass there on the way to the next stop`,`A line can keep to chosen platforms of a station, and to one side of the road at a bus stop`,`A wider Stops window: a stop opens to its platforms, side and freight orders, waypoints are rows of their own, and the lists of cargos show their icons`,`Noise and exhaust: lorries and trains are heard in the towns and lorries breathed, in two new needs, Little noise and Clean air, which houses and woods between soften`,`A new map in the analytics, Industries: every industry with the icons of what it takes and makes, and a line to where its goods go`,`Every cargo in a yard for goods lies in containers, bigger now, and the containers on wagons and lorries carry the emblem of their cargo, so what goes where can be seen at a glance`,`Forklifts drive out of the halls of the works to fetch from the yard, where containers, skips and crates now stand up from the ground`,`The ground of the lorries at a yard for goods runs to the road as one paved place, fenced in with the yard`]},{version:`0.4.3`,date:`2026-10-14`,changes:[`No two industries look alike: other sheds, heaps and roofs, pits and tips round a colliery, felled ground round a forestry, and a track between those that stand close`,`Passengers wait for the bus that goes their way: nobody gets on one that goes the long way round first`,`Lorries that only wait for a load give up their bay to one that has something to load or unload, and drive on past a full industry when they load at another stop too`,`A new map has a border of open land all round, so a city at the edge can be moved clear of the windows`,`The chart of a line shows the passengers on its busiest stretch, and lines over the same stops share them`,`A train, a bus or a lorry at the foot of a bridge is no longer drawn behind the ramp`,`The builders yard is T. I. Porton now, with its name on the roof`,`The question mark of an industry opens the page of that industry in the wiki`,`An industrial estate hums like works, and CrossCo and Flatpakk make no noise of machines`,`The fence of a logistics hub or an industrial station leaves the ground of the lorries free from the day it is built, not only after a look at build mode`]},{version:`0.4.2`,date:`2026-10-13`,changes:[`Buses no longer drive round a block for ever when their stop stands where two pieces of a road join`,`Of the buses and trains that wait for their turn at the first stop of a line, the one that came first leaves first`,`The Service button of a lorry sends it to its depot`]},{version:`0.4.1`,date:`2026-10-13`,changes:[`The drive of a logistics hub or an industrial station joins its road in a curve, with kerbs and a mouth at the road`,`Logistics hubs and industrial stations have a fence round them where one fits, and bushes outside it`]},{version:`0.4.0`,date:`2026-10-13`,changes:[`Food: farms grow produce, Pestlé, the food works, makes food of it, and CrossCo, the grocery store, sells it in the town itself`,`Towns need food in their shops, and a town that does well builds a new industry in its industrial estate, for all to see`,`Logistics hub: a big store for goods that trains and lorries fill and empty, with or without track, and with a depot beside it if you like`,`What a stop loads and unloads is chosen from a dropdown`,`What lies in a yard is seen: containers in the colour of their cargo, with its emblem on top`,`An industrial station serves industries within 150 m, and lorries turn in from a road that runs right past its yard`,`Power stations burn three times the coal`,`New maps: Flatpakk stands close to its town, and no industrial estate has two industries of the same kind`]},{version:`0.3.8`,date:`2026-10-13`,changes:[`Feedback and roadmap in the game`]},{version:`0.3.5`,date:`2026-10-13`,changes:[`Graphics options in the settings: resolution, frames a second, wind, and a slider for the size of the interface`,`Build mode, line mode and the analytics open at once`,`With the Lines window open, all lines are on the map; the one you point at stands out`,`Bus stops have a pin in build mode, so they are seen from far off`]},{version:`0.3.4`,date:`2026-10-12`,changes:[`A dropdown no longer opens behind its window`,`The time lapse runs more smoothly on big maps: the cars take less memory, and a slow moment is no longer followed by a long stop`]},{version:`0.3.3`,date:`2026-10-10`,changes:[`Industrial estates have jobs of their own: commuters go there, a stop there serves them, and the Journeys map shows them`,`Flatpakk is closed on Sunday: nobody drives there, and its lights are out at night and after it closes at eight`,`Continue and loading a save show the loading screen until the map is drawn and the game is ready to run`,`Big maps run more smoothly: less to draw from far off, less memory, and shorter stops when a town builds a road`]},{version:`0.3.2`,date:`2026-10-10`,changes:[`Freight pays: more by the tonne and the kilometre, a sum for every tonne carried at all, and trains and lorries wait for a load instead of running empty`,`Finance keeps freight apart from the fares: a line of its own, a chart, and the freight lines in their own list with their tonnes`,`A pin beside every vehicle, stop, depot, industry and town moves the map to it, and a vehicle's card has a Follow button`,`What is selected or pointed at is framed by its footprint, in place of a circle`,`A loading screen with a bar while the game starts, and a bar while a map is being made`,`A slip road merges into the road it joins at whatever angle it comes in`,`What a line runs as is chosen in two rows: Rail and Bus in blue, Freight and Lorry in orange`,`In the window of an industry, a row shows an arrow on the map: where its cargo comes from or goes to`]},{version:`0.3.1`,date:`2026-10-09`,changes:[`Cars drive to a parking spot of their own at Flatpakk and the industries, and back out of it`,`Flatpakk draws shoppers: most after work and at the weekend, until it closes at eight`,`New maps: a power station at every big city, and a bigger map has more cities and industries by itself; the form asks for fewer or more, not for a number`,`New maps: nothing meets a highway but its exits, no two Flatpakk stand near each other, and Flatpakk stands nearer the exit`,`Warehouses in the industrial estates: big halls in place of rows of thin sheds`,`Industries and Flatpakk stand on the land itself, with no box of ground under them; Flatpakk has trees and hedges round it`,`Power lines blend into the land: faint from far off, and their pylons come in gently as you zoom in`,`The bus depot is called vehicle depot: lorries use it too, and the lorries that belong to nobody are plain white`]},{version:`0.3.0`,date:`2026-10-09`,changes:[`Industries work: forestry, sawmill, furniture works and more make cargo from what they take, grow when they are served well, and have a window of their own`,`Freight trains and lorries: each stop is told what to load and what to unload, paid by the tonne and the kilometre`,`Lorries drive in at the gate of an industry and back into a free loading bay, trailer first`,`Power: power stations burn coal and send power to their towns over lines on pylons`,`Big towns need furniture in their shops, building materials and power to keep growing`,`Bigger maps: a new Large with twice the ground, and cities in all sizes`,`Industrial estates: bigger cities have a quarter of workshops, yards and car parks, and Flatpakk, the furniture store, stands by the highway`,`Industrial stations show what lies in their yard, and their crane moves to the wagon it loads`]},{version:`0.2.4`,date:`2026-10-09`,changes:[`Finance in tabs: every line of the books opens into what it is made of, with charts by the hour and the day, the books of each line, and the chart of a stop in the colours of its lines`,`Regions and districts: every city has a region, its districts are real pieces of the town between its main roads, and the analytics have a Regions map`,`The Journeys map shows how many travel between towns as bands, in place of arrows`,`Buildings: walls under flat roofs, shadows from the foot, lit windows that go out as it gets late, and trees, benches and planters in town centres`,`Lights: headlights throw a beam, high beams in open country, and rear lights that light up when a car or bus brakes`,`Traffic: more kinds of car, cars that keep to their lane, and Quiet roads of a town counts the cars held up in its streets`]},{version:`0.2.3`,date:`2026-10-08`,changes:[`Wiki: how everything in the game works, by topic and with a search, from the top bar and the main menu`,`A click on a question mark opens what it is about in the wiki`]},{version:`0.2.2`,date:`2026-10-08`,changes:[`The map moves with W, A, S and D or the arrow keys`,`Tractors drive smoothly when the map is zoomed out and time runs fast`,`In build mode, Demolish on something that is only planned takes it out of the plan at once`]},{version:`0.2.1`,date:`2026-10-08`,changes:[`Stops have a rating: it falls where people wait long, fewer then set out from there, some give up, and the town is less satisfied`,`Point at a destination in a card to see the way there as an arrow on the map, at a line anywhere to see it, and at a stop in a list to find it`,`A station that is made bigger gets its new tracks away from its building, which stays where it is with its car park`,`Analytics: maps of traffic, journeys, hot zones, coverage, delays, noise and pollution, as the average of a day or by the hour`,`In build mode, traffic, delays, noise and pollution can be laid over the plan from the corner`,`Buses carry fewer of the trips and cost more to run`,`Statistics in the main menu: time played, rides, distances, what you built and spent, and your best days`,`Build mode shows what is still being built as it will stand, so that it can be built on`]},{version:`0.2.0`,date:`2026-10-07`,changes:[`Difficulty: Simple, or Realistic, where what you build takes time to build`,`Building sites with machines, people and sound; bridges go up on piers and tunnels are dug`,`Towns that live: people come and go by how satisfied they are, and towns build lanes, houses and squares, round the forests, and build denser where they have no ground left`,`Gardens with fences, hedges, bushes and flowers, and houses that stand on open ground`,`A window for every town, by a click on its name`,`Line style: sixteen colours, and a second colour as dashes or stripes`,`The list of lines by kind, and a line pointed at is shown on the map`,`Vehicles can be bought while their depot is still being built`,`No more stutter when a vehicle is bought, a schedule is changed or something is built`]},{version:`0.1.6`,date:`2026-10-07`,changes:[`Stations with their tracks in pairs: a platform either side of each pair`,`Through station: two tracks in the middle on which trains pass without stopping`,`A roof over all the tracks of the biggest stations, with windows that show the trains`,`Fixed: trains and buses that waited for hours at their first stop after one of the line had parked in a yard`]},{version:`0.1.5`,date:`2026-10-07`,changes:[`Stations and depots line themselves up with the road, track or station beside them`,`Rotate: the mouse wheel with Shift held, or the Rotate button`,`Stations and depots with up to six tracks`,`A station being placed shows its forecourt and car park`,`Stations and depots stop before roads and houses; put fully on them, those are demolished, at a price`,`Escape stops what is going on: what is being placed, build mode, the window on top`,`Sound of crowds where many people wait, and in the middle of a city`,`Sound of bus doors at stops`]},{version:`0.1.3`,date:`2026-10-06`,changes:[`New world generation: smaller towns that have grown street by street`,`Livelier towns: lanes that just end, houses along every street`,`Line routes: the real way of a line on the map, with moving arrows`,`Buses in stronger colours, the other traffic toned down`,`Zoom in twice as far`,`People on the streets stay in view longer when zooming out`,`Bought vehicles show in the Vehicles window at once`,`Versions: this list, in the main menu and in the settings`]},{version:`0.1.2`,date:`2026-10-06`,changes:[`Buses: bus stops, bus depots and lines for buses`,`Changing: passengers change between lines where stops stand close together`,`Tutorial: a first bus line, step by step`,`Traffic lights at big junctions`,`People in the towns, at stops and on platforms`,`Station forecourts`,`Less blocky cities on new maps`]},{version:`0.1.1`,date:`2026-10-05`,changes:[`Days and weeks, with rush hours`,`Schedules for lines`,`Cars on the roads`,`Finance window and a bank`,`Sound, with a mixer`,`Main menu`]},{version:`0.1.0`,date:`2026-10-04`,changes:[`First public version`,`Track, stations, lines, trains, signals and depots`,`Maps from a seed: cities, roads, water, industries`,`Roads to build`,`Tunnels and viaducts`]}];export{e as RELEASES};